hadiths[602]{hadithnumber,text}:
"993","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما narrated: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to go out to al-Mughammas to relieve himself.""** Nāfiʿ added, ""It is approximately two miles from Makkah."""
"994","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما narrated: Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to relieve himself, he would go far away. One day he set out to relieve himself, then performed ablution and put on one of his leather socks (khuff). A green bird suddenly flew down, seized the other sock, soared into the sky with it, and dropped it, whereupon a black venomous snake fell out from inside it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remarked, ""This is an honor with which Allah has blessed me."" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated: > **""O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of whatever crawls upon its belly, from the evil of whatever walks upon two legs, and from the evil of whatever walks upon four.""**"
"995","Bilāl ibn al-Ḥārith رضي الله عنه narrated: We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his journeys. He went out to relieve himself—and whenever he went to relieve himself, he would go to a distant place. I brought him a vessel of water and followed him, but then I heard men disputing with clamor and noise such as I had never heard before. When he returned, he said, ""Is that Bilāl?"" I replied, ""It is Bilāl."" He asked, ""Do you have water with you?"" I replied, ""Yes."" He said, ""You did well."" He took it from me and performed ablution. I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I heard near you men disputing and shouting in clamor, and I could not understand anyone from their languages."" He ﷺ said: > **""The Muslim jinn and the polytheist jinn were disputing before me; they asked me to designate dwellings for them, so I settled the Muslims in al-Jals (the uplands, villages, and mountains) and settled the polytheists in al-Ghawr (the lowlands between the mountains and the sea).""**"
"996","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to seek out a suitable, soft spot for his urination just as he would seek out a suitable place for his encampment.""**"
"997","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: > **""Beware of the three acts that incur curses.""** It was said, ""What are the acts that incur curses, O Messenger of Allah?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""That one of you sits [to relieve himself] in shade sought for shelter, or in a walkway, or in a pool of collected water.""**"
"998","Jābir رضي الله عنه narrated: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade urinating in flowing water.""**"
"999","Bakr ibn Māʿiz narrated: I heard ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd رضي الله عنه narrate that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Urine must not be left standing in a basin within the house, for the angels do not enter a house wherein urine is left standing; and do not ever urinate in your place of bathing.""**"
"1000","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما narrated: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that a person relieve himself beneath a fruit-bearing tree, and he forbade relieving oneself on the bank of a flowing river.""**"
"1001","Ḥudhayfah ibn Asīd رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whoever harms the Muslims in their pathways, their curse becomes incumbent upon him.""**"
"1002","Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn reported: A man said to Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه, ""You have given us religious rulings on everything, and you are nearly ready to give us rulings even about defecation!"" Thereupon Abū Hurayrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Whoever discharges his feces upon a path among the paths of the Muslims, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all of mankind.""**"
"1003","Abū Bakrah رضي الله عنه said: > **""It is disliked for a man to urinate in his bathing place, because obsessive misgivings (waswās) arise from it.""**"
"1004","Surāqah ibn Mālik ibn Juʿshum رضي الله عنه narrated: Whenever he returned from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would teach and instruct his people. One day, a man said to him playfully in jest, ""Nothing remains for Surāqah except to teach you how to defecate!"" Surāqah replied: > **""When you go out to relieve yourselves, avoid sitting in the shade or in pathways; take cleansing stones with you, lean firmly upon your shins [and left side], cleanse yourselves with stones, and use an odd number.""**"
"1005","ʿAlqamah narrated: A man from the polytheists said to ʿAbdullāh [ibn Masʿūd] رضي الله عنه, ""I believe your companion has taught you everything, even teaching you how to relieve yourselves!"" ʿAbdullāh replied, ""Even if you say so mockingly, he has indeed taught us: > **""Not to face the Qiblah with our private parts, not to clean ourselves with our right hands, not to clean ourselves with dung, not to clean ourselves with bone, and not to clean ourselves with fewer than three stones.""**"
"1006","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The barrier between the eyes of the jinn and the private parts of the children of Adam when they take off their garments is to say: 'Bismillāh' (In the name of Allah).""**"
"1007","Yaʿlā ibn Siyābah رضي الله عنه narrated: > **""I was with the Prophet ﷺ on one of his journeys when he intended to relieve himself. He commanded two small palm saplings, and they came together until one joined the other [to screen him]. Then, when he had finished, he commanded them, and they returned to the places where they had grown.""**"
"1008","Sahl ibn Ḥunayf رضي الله عنه narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""You are an emissary to the people of Makkah, so say: 'Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sends you greetings of peace and commands you with three things: do not swear by other than Allah; when you relieve yourselves, do not face the Qiblah nor turn your backs to it; and do not clean yourselves with bone or animal dung.'""**"
"1009","A man from the Anṣār reported from his father رضي الله عنه: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from facing either of the two Qiblahs (Makkah or Jerusalem) while urinating or defecating.""**"
"1010","Nāfiʿ reported that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr al-ʿAjlānī narrated to ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar from his father [ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb] رضي الله عنه: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade facing either of the two Qiblahs when defecating or urinating.""**"
"1011","Sahl ibn Saʿd رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When one of you goes to relieve himself, he should neither face the Qiblah nor turn his back to it.""**"
"1012","ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Jazʾ al-Zubaydī رضي الله عنه reported: > **""I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinating while facing the Qiblah, and I was the first one to relate that to the people.""**"
"1013","ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir رضي الله عنه reported: > **""I saw the Prophet ﷺ facing the Qiblah after the prohibition while defecating or urinating.""**"
"1014","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever neither faces the Qiblah nor turns his back toward it while defecating, a good deed will be recorded for him and an evil deed will be erased from him.""**"
"1015","ʿUmar [ibn al-Khaṭṭāb] رضي الله عنه said: > **""I have never urinated while standing since I embraced Islam.""**"
"1016","Sahl ibn Saʿd رضي الله عنه reported: > **""He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinating while standing.""**"
"1017","Ibn Sīrīn narrated: While Saʿd [ibn ʿUbādah] رضي الله عنه was urinating standing, he leaned over and died. The jinn had struck him, and they chanted: > **""We killed the chieftain of the Khazraj, Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah; we shot him with two arrows and did not miss his heart.""**"
"1018","Qatādah narrated: Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah رضي الله عنه stood up to urinate, then returned and said, ""Indeed, I feel something in my back."" It was not long before he passed away. Thereupon the jinn lamented, chanting: > **""We killed the chieftain of the Khazraj, Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah; and we shot him with an arrow and it did not miss his heart.""**"
"1019","Jābir رضي الله عنه reported: > **""Whenever the Prophet ﷺ intended to relieve himself, he would not raise his garment until he drew close to the ground.""**"
"1020","A man from Banū Mudlij reported from his father: Surāqah ibn Mālik ibn Juʿshum رضي الله عنه returned from the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us such-and-such."" A man said mockingly, ""Did he even teach you how to defecate?"" Surāqah replied, ""Yes, by the One Who sent him with the truth! > **""He commanded us to lean upon the left [foot] and keep the right [foot] upright.""**"
"1021","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Two persons must not go out together to defecate, sitting and conversing while exposing their private parts, for indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, detests that.""**"
"1022","Jābir رضي الله عنه reported: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade laughing at passing wind.""**"
"1023","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها narrated: The Prophet ﷺ passed by two graves whose occupants were being punished, so he said: > **""Indeed, they are being punished, and they are not being punished for something difficult to avoid: one of them did not protect himself from urine [splatters], while the other used to spread malicious gossip (namīmah).""** He then called for a fresh palm branch, snapped it in two, placed a piece on this grave and on that grave, and said: > **""May it lighten their punishment as long as they do not dry up.""**"
"1024","ʿĪsā ibn Yazdād narrated from his father رضي الله عنه that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When one of you urinates, let him shake his penis three times.""** Zamʿah said, ""Once is sufficient."""
"1025","Anas [ibn Mālik] رضي الله عنه reported: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man being punished in his grave on account of malicious gossip, and he passed by another man being punished in his grave on account of urine.""**"
"1026","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Most of the punishment of the grave is due to urine, so purify and protect yourselves from urine.""**"
"1027","Abū Bakrah رضي الله عنه narrated: While the Prophet ﷺ was walking between me and another man, he came upon two graves and said, ""The dwellers of these two graves are being punished; bring me a palm branch."" Abū Bakrah said: My companion and I raced, and I brought him a palm branch. He split it into two halves, placing one upon this grave and one upon that grave, and said: > **""May their punishment be lightened as long as these two remain fresh. Indeed, they are being punished for matters that were not difficult to avoid: backbiting (ghībah) and urine [splatters].""**"
"1028","ʿUbādah [ibn al-Ṣāmit] رضي الله عنه narrated: We asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about urine, and he said: > **""If any of it touches you, wash it off; for indeed, I consider that punishment of the grave stems from it.""**"
"1029","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه narrated: The Prophet ﷺ went out on a scorching hot day toward Baqīʿ al-Gharqad. The people were walking behind him, and when he heard the sound of their sandals, it weighed upon his soul, so he sat down until he let them precede him so that no pride might enter his heart. When he reached Baqīʿ al-Gharqad, there were two graves wherein two men had just been buried. The Prophet ﷺ halted and asked, ""Whom did you bury here today?"" They said, ""So-and-so and so-and-so."" They asked, ""O Prophet of Allah, what is the matter?"" He replied: > **""As for one of them, he did not protect himself from urine; and as for the other, he used to spread malicious gossip.""** He then took a fresh palm branch, split it, and placed it upon the two graves. They asked, ""O Prophet of Allah, why did you do that?"" He said: > **""So that their punishment may be alleviated.""** They asked, ""O Prophet of Allah, until when will they be punished?"" He said: > **""It is an unseen matter known only to Allah. Were it not for the wavering of your hearts and your excessive talking, you would surely hear what I hear.""**"
"1030","Anas [ibn Mālik] رضي الله عنه narrated: The Prophet ﷺ passed by two graves belonging to Banū al-Najjār whose occupants were being punished for malicious gossip and urine. He took a palm leaf stalk, split it, and placed one half upon this grave and the other half upon that grave, saying: > **""Their punishment will continue to be lightened as long as these two remain fresh.""**"
"1031","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما narrated: One day, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by some graves carrying a fresh palm stalk. He split it into two, placed one on a grave and the other on another grave, and then walked on. We asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, why did you do that?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""As for one of them, he was being punished for malicious gossip; and as for the other, he did not take precautions against urine. They will not be punished as long as these remain fresh.""**"
"1032","Shufayy ibn Mātiʿ al-Aṣbaḥī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There are four persons who inflict additional torment upon the inhabitants of the Fire beyond the torment they already endure; they rush back and forth between scalding water and Hellfire, crying out in ruin and destruction. The dwellers of Hell say to one another, 'What is the matter with these individuals that they torment us on top of our existing anguish?' One of them is locked inside a coffin of glowing embers; another drags his bowels behind him; another has pus and blood gushing from his mouth; and another eats his own flesh. It is said concerning the man in the coffin, 'What was the matter with this wretched soul that he torments us on top of our anguish?' It will be answered, 'Indeed, this wretched soul died while bearing debts of people's wealth, finding no way to settle or fulfill them.' Then it is said concerning the one dragging his bowels, 'What was the matter with this wretched soul that he torments us on top of our anguish?' He will answer, 'Indeed, this wretched soul did not care where urine splattered on him, and he would never wash it off.' Then it is said concerning the one whose mouth gushes with pus and blood, 'What was the matter with this wretched soul that he torments us on top of our anguish?' He will answer, 'Indeed, this wretched soul used to eat the flesh of people [through backbiting and slander].'""**"
"1033","Muʿādh ibn Jabal رضي الله عنه reported: > **""The Prophet ﷺ used to take meticulous care to protect himself from urine, and he would command his Companions to do so.""** Muʿādh added, ""Indeed, the majority of the grave's punishment stems from urine."""
"1034","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Beware of urine, for indeed it is the very first matter for which a servant will be called to account in the grave.""**"
"1035","Maymūnah bint Saʿd رضي الله عنها narrated: She asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, instruct us: from what does the punishment of the grave stem?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""From the traces of urine; so whoever is splattered by urine, let him wash it, and if he finds no water, let him wipe it with clean earth.""**"
"1036","Abū Mūsā [al-Ashʿarī] رضي الله عنه narrated: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinating while seated, widening the space between his thighs so much that I felt sympathy for him on account of the prolonged sitting. Then he approached, forming the number sixty-three with his fingers, and said: > **""The people of the Children of Israel were far stricter concerning urine than you: a man among them would carry shears, and if any urine touched his garment, he would cut it out.""**"
"1037","ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Jazʾ رضي الله عنه reported: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade anyone from cleaning himself with a bone, animal dung, or charcoal.""**"
"1038","Al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām رضي الله عنه narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the Fajr prayer in the mosque of Madīnah. When he finished, he asked, ""Which of you will accompany me to the delegation of the jinn tonight?"" The people remained silent and no one spoke. He asked this three times. Then he walked past me, took me by my hand, and I walked along with him until all the mountains of Madīnah disappeared from our sight, and we reached an open, barren land. Suddenly, there were tall men resembling spears, tucking their garments between their legs. When I saw them, a severe trembling overcame me such that my legs could barely support me out of terror. When we drew near them, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew a line in the ground with his big toe and said to me, ""Sit in the middle of it."" When I sat down, all the fear and doubt I had been experiencing departed from me. The Prophet ﷺ went forward between me and them, reciting the Qur’an in an elevated voice until dawn broke. Then he approached, passed by me, and said, ""Follow."" I began walking with him, and before we had gone far, he said to me, ""Turn and look: do you see anyone where those beings were?"" I replied, ""O Messenger of Allah, I see a vast multitude of dark figures."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ bowed his head toward the earth, joined a bone to a piece of animal dung, threw it toward them, and said: > **""This is guidance from me for them: they are a delegation from a people—the delegation of Naṣībīn. They asked me for sustenance, so I assigned to them every bone and animal dung.""** Al-Zubayr added, ""Therefore, it is never permissible for anyone to clean himself with a bone or animal dung."""
"1039","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked me to accompany him one night, saying: > **""A group of fifteen jinn—cousins and nephew-brothers to one another—are coming to me tonight so that I may recite the Qur’an to them.""** I set out with him to the place he intended. He drew a line for me, made me sit down, and said, ""Do not step outside of this."" I stayed within it throughout the night until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned to me at dawn, holding an old dry bone, animal dung, and charcoal in his hand, and he said: > **""When you go to relieve yourself, do not clean yourself with any of these.""** ʿAbdullāh said: When morning arrived, I said to myself, ""I must see where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had been."" So I went there and saw a clearing large enough for seventy camels."
"1040","Wāthilah ibn al-Asqaʿ رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""None of you should say: 'I poured out water' [meaning urination], but rather let him say: 'I am urinating.'""**"
"1041","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""When one of you cleanses himself with stones, let him use an odd number; indeed, Allah is Witr (One) and loves what is odd. Do you not see that the heavens are seven, the earths are seven, and the circumambulation (Ṭawāf) is seven?""** He mentioned several other things as well."
"1042","Jābir رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When one of you cleanses himself with stones, let him cleanse with three.""** And in another narration: > **""When one of you defecates, let him wipe three times.""**"
"1043","ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir رضي الله عنه reported: > **""Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ applied kohl, he applied it an odd number of times; and whenever he cleansed himself with stones, he cleansed an odd number of times.""**"
"1044","Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When one of you defecates, let him wipe with three stones, for indeed that is sufficient for him.""**"
"1045","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported in a marfūʿ narration that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whoever cleanses himself with stones, let him cleanse with three.""**"
"1046","Ṭāriq ibn ʿAbdillāh رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When you cleanse yourselves with stones, make it an odd number; and when you perform ablution, blow the water out from your nose.""**"
"1047","Al-Sāʾib Abū Khallād رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""When one of you enters the privy [to relieve himself], let him wipe with three stones.""**"
"1048","Sahl ibn Saʿd رضي الله عنه narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked concerning istinjāʾ (cleansing after relieving oneself), and he said: > **""Can one of you not find three stones: two stones for the buttocks and one stone for the anal passage?""**"
"1049","ʿAlqamah reported: A man from the polytheists said to ʿAbdullāh [ibn Masʿūd] رضي الله عنه, ""I believe your companion has taught you everything, even teaching you how to relieve yourselves!"" ʿAbdullāh replied, ""Even if you say so mockingly, he has indeed taught us: > **""Not to face the Qiblah with our private parts, not to clean ourselves with our right hands, not to clean ourselves with animal dung, not to clean ourselves with bone, and not to clean ourselves with fewer than three stones.""**"
"1050","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, Allah is Witr (One) and loves what is odd; so when you cleanse yourselves with stones, make it an odd number.""**"
"1051","ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr رضي الله عنهما said: > **""They did not use to wash their private parts with water [relying instead upon stones].""**"
"1052","ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه urinated, then wiped his penis with earth, turned to us, and said: > **""Thus were we taught.""**"
"1053","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما narrated: When this verse was revealed concerning the people of Qubāʾ: {""Within it are men who love to purify themselves; and Allah loves those who purify themselves""} [al-Tawbah: 108], the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked them [concerning their practice], and they said: > **""We follow stones with water [for purification].""**"
"1054","ʿUwaym ibn Sāʿidah رضي الله عنه narrated: The Prophet ﷺ came to them at the mosque of Qubāʾ and said: > **""Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, has praised you excellently regarding purification in the account of your mosque. What is this purification that you perform?""** They said, ""By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, we know nothing other than that we had Jewish neighbors who used to wash their rears after defecation, so we washed as they washed."""
"1055","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما narrated: When this verse was revealed: {""Within it are men who love to purify themselves""} [al-Tawbah: 108], the Prophet ﷺ sent for ʿUwaym ibn Sāʿidah رضي الله عنه and asked: > **""What is this purification for which Allah has praised you?""** They said, ""O Messenger of Allah, not a single man or woman among us comes out after defecating except that they wash their private part [or rear]."" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""It is precisely this.""**"
"1056","ʿAbdullāh ibn Salām رضي الله عنه said: ""O Messenger of Allah, before your coming we were People of the Scripture, and we were commanded to wash after defecating and urinating."" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, Allah has become pleased with you, has praised you, and has loved you.""**"
"1057","Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Salām reported from his father [ʿAbdullāh ibn Salām] رضي الله عنه: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to the mosque founded upon piety—the mosque of Qubāʾ—stood at its entrance, and said: > **""Indeed, Allah has praised you excellently regarding purification. What is your manner of purification?""** We said, ""O Messenger of Allah, we were People of the Scripture, and we found cleansing with water enjoined upon us, and we still practice it today."" He ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has praised you excellently regarding purification, saying: {'Within it are men who love to purify themselves; and Allah loves those who purify themselves'} [al-Tawbah: 108].""**"
"1058","Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Salām narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us—meaning at Qubāʾ—and said: > **""Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has praised you with good regarding purification; will you not inform me?""** He meant Allah's saying: {""Within it are men who love to purify themselves; and Allah loves those who purify themselves""} [al-Tawbah: 108]. They said: > **""O Messenger of Allah, we find it prescribed for us in the Torah""—meaning cleansing with water.**"
"1059","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""O people of Qubāʾ, what is this purification with which you have been specifically honored in this verse: {'Within it are men who love to purify themselves; and Allah loves those who purify themselves'} [al-Tawbah: 108]?""** They replied, ""O Messenger of Allah, none of us comes out after defecating except that he washes his rear."""
"1060","Khuzaymah ibn Thābit رضي الله عنه reported: > **""Men from among us used to wash off the traces of excrement after defecating, so this verse was revealed regarding them: {'Within it are men who love to purify themselves'} [al-Tawbah: 108].""**"
"1061","Abū Ayyūb [al-Anṣārī] رضي الله عنه reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: > **""Who are those concerning whom Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: {'Within it are men who love to purify themselves; and Allah loves those who purify themselves'} [al-Tawbah: 108]?""** He ﷺ said: > **""They used to cleanse themselves with water, and they would not sleep through the entire night [spending parts of it in prayer].""**"
"1062","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها said: > **""A woman washing her anterior private part [after urination] is from the Sunnah.""**"
"1063","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما narrated: One of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ performed ghusl from ritual impurity (janābah), and the Prophet ﷺ began performing ablution with the water left over from it. She mentioned that to him, whereupon he said: > **""Indeed, nothing renders water impure.""**"
"1064","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported: The Prophet ﷺ intended to perform ablution, so one of his wives said to him, ""I have already performed ablution from this water."" Yet he performed ablution from it and said: > **""Indeed, nothing renders water impure.""**"
"1065","Maymūnah رضي الله عنها reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Nothing renders water impure.""**"
"1066","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Nothing renders water impure.""**"
"1067","Muʿādhah reported: I asked ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها regarding performing ghusl from ritual impurity (janābah) [using leftover water], and she replied: > **""Indeed, nothing renders water impure.""**"
"1068","Abū Umāmah al-Bāhilī رضي الله عنه narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Nothing renders water impure except that which alters its odor or its taste.""**"
"1069","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Water is not made impure by anything.""**"
"1070","Muʿādh ibn Jabal رضي الله عنه narrated: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to perform ablution with water as long as it has not become stale and discolored—turning green or yellow.""**"
"1071","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما said: I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, is performing ablution from a new, covered earthen jar more beloved to you, or from common ablution vessels (al-maṭāhir)?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: > **""No, rather from the common ablution vessels; indeed, the religion of Allah is upright and accommodating (al-Ḥanīfiyyah al-Samḥah).""** He [Ibn ʿUmar] added: ""And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would send for water from the common ablution vessels, and it would be brought to him and he would drink from it, seeking the blessings of the Muslims' hands."""
"1072","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها narrated: ""I heated some water in the sun and brought it to the Prophet ﷺ so that he might perform ablution with it. Thereupon, he said: > **""Do not do that, O ʿĀʾishah, for it causes vitiligo (al-bayaḍ).""**"""
"1073","Salamah ibn al-Akwaʿ رضي الله عنه reported: > **Water used to be heated for him, and he would perform ablution with it.**"
"1074","Ḥumayd ibn Hilāl narrated: Abū Rifāʿah رضي الله عنه used to warm water for his companions and then say: > **""Perform your ablution thoroughly with this [warm water], and I shall perform mine thoroughly with this,""** and he would then perform his ablution using cold water."
"1075","Muʿāwiyah رضي الله عنه said: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ instructed me not to approach my wife intimately on the first night of the crescent moon, not to perform ablution from a copper vessel, and to clean my teeth with the tooth-stick whenever I awaken from my sleep.""**"
"1076","Muʿādh ibn Jabal رضي الله عنه reported: > **He used to assist the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in performing ablution from a wooden cup clamped with copper, and he would give him water to drink from it.**"
"1077","ʿIkrimah رحمه الله said: > **""Nabīdh serves as water for ablution for one who finds nothing else.""** Al-Awzāʿī رحمه الله commented: > **""If it is intoxicating, then do not perform ablution with it.""**"
"1078","ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mughīrah ibn Abī Burdah al-Kinānī narrated that a man from Banū Mudlij informed him: They used to embark on rafts at sea for fishing, carrying some fresh water with them for drinking. The time for prayer arrived while they were out at sea, so they mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ and said: ""If we perform ablution with our fresh drinking water, we will suffer from thirst; but if we perform ablution with sea water, we feel unease in our hearts."" The Prophet ﷺ said to them: > **""Its water is pure and purifying, and its dead creatures are lawful to eat.""**"
"1079","ʿAbdullāh al-Mudlijī رضي الله عنه narrated that he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, we are people who ride rafts at sea, and we carry water only for our drinking."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: > **""Its water is pure and purifying, and its dead creatures are lawful to eat.""**"
"1080","Al-ʿArakī [the sailor] رضي الله عنه narrated that he asked the Prophet ﷺ about sea water, to which he ﷺ replied: > **""Its water is pure and purifying, and its dead creatures are lawful to eat.""**"
"1081","Mūsā ibn Salamah narrated: ""Sinān ibn Salamah and I performed the Pilgrimage. When we arrived in Makkah, I said, 'Come with us to Ibn ʿAbbās.' So we entered upon him, and I asked him concerning sea water. He replied: > **""The water of the sea is purifying.""**"""
"1082","Mūsā ibn Salamah also narrated: ""Sinān ibn Salamah instructed me to ask Ibn ʿAbbās about sea water and about which part of the month I should fast. So I went to Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما and said: 'My brother instructed me to ask you about performing ablution with sea water.' He replied: > **""They are both seas; it causes you no harm whichever of the two you perform ablution with.""** I asked: 'And during which part of the month should I fast?' He said: > **""The White Days (the 13th, 14th, and 15th of the lunar month).""** I asked: 'We participate in these military expeditions and acquire captives; may I emancipate a slave on behalf of my mother even though she did not instruct me to do so?' He replied: > **""Emancipate on behalf of your mother.""**"""
"1083","Anas رضي الله عنه reported: > **""The Prophet ﷺ used to perform ablution with the water remaining from moistening his tooth-stick.""**"
"1084","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to an area in Madinah called Buṭḥān and said: ""O Anas, pour water for my ablution."" So I poured water for him. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had relieved himself, he approached the vessel, but a cat came and drank from the vessel. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ paused for it until the cat had finished drinking, and then he performed his ablution. I mentioned the matter of the cat to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, whereupon he said: > **""O Anas, the cat is part of the household fixtures; it will never defile anything nor make it impure.""**"
"1085","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها narrated: > **""A cat would pass by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he would tilt the vessel towards it so that it might drink from it, and then he would perform ablution with what was left over.""**"
"1086","ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Qatādah reported from his father, Abū Qatādah رضي الله عنه: Ablution water was set down for him, and a cat drank from it. He then proceeded to perform ablution with it, so they said, ""O Abū Qatādah, the cat has lapped from it!"" He replied, ""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""The cat is of the folk of the house, and it is among those who roam around you, male and female.""**"""
"1087","Al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah رضي الله عنه narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked me for water, so I came upon a tent wherein there was a Bedouin woman. I said to her: ""This is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking water for ablution; do you have any water?"" She said: ""May my father and mother be ransomed for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ! By Allah, the sky does not shade nor does the earth carry a soul more beloved to me than his soul, nor more precious. However, this waterskin is made from the hide of an unslaughtered dead animal, and I would hate to make the Messenger of Allah ﷺ impure with it."" I returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him, whereupon he said: > **""Return to her; if she has tanned it, then that is its purification.""** He [al-Mughīrah] said: ""So I returned to her and mentioned that to her, and she said, 'Yes, by Allah, I have tanned it.' Thereupon, I brought him water from it."""
"1088","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه narrated: The Prophet ﷺ requested water for ablution, and it was said to him: ""We could not find any except in a waterskin made from the hide of an unslaughtered carcass."" He asked: > **""Did you tan it?""** They replied: ""Yes."" He ﷺ said: > **""Then bring it, for indeed that is its purification.""**"
"1089","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out on one of his military expeditions and passed by the homes of some Arabs. He sent word to them: ""Is there any water for the ablution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"" They replied: ""We have no water except in the hide of a dead animal that we tanned with milk."" The Prophet ﷺ sent word to them: > **""Its tanning is its purification.""** So it was brought to him, and he performed ablution with it and prayed."
"1090","Anas رضي الله عنه narrated: I was walking with the Prophet ﷺ when he said to me: ""O my little son, ask for water for ablution for me from this household."" So I said [to the residents]: ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ is asking for water for ablution."" A man replied: ""Inform him that our bucket is made from the skin of an unslaughtered carcass."" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Ask them: Did you tan it?""** They replied: ""Yes."" He ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, its tanning is its purification.""**"
"1091","Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a dead sheep and said: > **""What harm would it have caused its owners had they benefited from its hide?""**"
"1092","Sinān ibn Salamah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Prophet ﷺ came upon a dead young sheep and said: > **""What harm would it have caused its owners had they benefited from its skin?""**"
"1093","Thābit narrated: I was sitting with ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā when a large man approached and asked, ""O Abū ʿĪsā?"" He replied, ""Yes."" The man said, ""Narrate to us what you heard regarding fur garments (al-firāʾ)."" He replied: ""I heard my father say: 'I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a man came and asked: ""O Messenger of Allah, may I pray in fur garments?"" The Prophet ﷺ replied: > **""Then where does tanning stand [in purifying it]?""**'"""
"1094","Jābir رضي الله عنه narrated: > **""Along with the Prophet ﷺ, we used to obtain waterskins and vessels among our spoils from the polytheists, and we would divide them among ourselves even though they were all made from [the hides of] unslaughtered animals.""**"
"1095","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها narrated: We had a sheep that we used to milk. The Prophet ﷺ noticed its absence and asked: ""What happened to your sheep?"" They said: ""It died."" He asked: ""What did you do with its hide?"" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah, we threw it away."" He ﷺ said: > **""Could you not have benefited from it? For indeed, tanning it serves as its lawful slaughter; it becomes lawful just as vinegar becomes lawful from wine.""**"
"1096","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها narrated: ""I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: > **""There is no harm in using the skin of an unslaughtered carcass once it has been tanned.""**"""
"1097","Umm Muslim al-Ashjaʿiyyah رضي الله عنها narrated that the Prophet ﷺ visited her while she was inside a domed leather tent, and he said: > **""How fine it would be if there were no [untanned] carcass hide in it!""** She said: ""So I began inspecting and removing [or cutting out] those parts."""
"1098","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUkaym رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Do not make use of the hide or sinew of an unslaughtered carcass.""**"
"1099","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما narrated: A man asked, ""How much water is sufficient for me for ablution?"" He replied, ""A mudd."" The man asked, ""How much water is sufficient for me for the ritual bath (ghusl)?"" He replied, ""A ṣāʿ."" The man said, ""That is not enough for me!"" Ibn ʿAbbās retorted: > **""May you be deprived of your mother! It was sufficient for one who was far better than you: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.""**"
"1100","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""A mudd suffices for ablution, and a ṣāʿ suffices for the ritual bath.""**"
"1101","Ibn ʿAbbās and ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنهم reported: > **""The Prophet ﷺ used to perform ablution with a mudd and perform the ritual bath with a ṣāʿ.""**"
"1102","ʿUqbah narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه that the Prophet ﷺ said similar to it: > **""A mudd suffices for ablution, and a ṣāʿ suffices for the ritual bath.""**"
"1103","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The ritual bath is performed with a ṣāʿ, and ablution with a mudd.""**"
"1104","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها narrated: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ablution [for prayer] with a small earthen pitcher (kūz al-ḥubb)—meaning that such an amount of water was sufficient for him.""**"
"1105","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها narrated: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ablution with a mudd and perform the ritual bath with a ṣāʿ.""**"
"1106","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه narrated: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution with half a mudd of water.""**"
"1107","Umm Kulthūm bint ʿAbdillāh ibn Zamʿah narrated that her grandmother Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, handed her a brass washbasin and said: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to take a ritual bath from this.""** And it held approximately a ṣāʿ of water or less."
"1108","Abū al-Dardāʾ رضي الله عنه reported: > **""The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution from a vessel beside a river, and when he finished, he poured the surplus water back into the river.""**"
"1109","Abū al-Dardāʾ رضي الله عنه narrated that the Prophet ﷺ passed by a river, took some water with a wooden bowl that he had with him, and then said: > **""May Allah convey it to a people whom He will benefit through it.""**"
"1110","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When one of you awakens from his sleep, let him not dip his hand into the vessel until he has washed it, for he does not know where his hand rested during the night; and let him mention the Name of Allah (say Bismillāh) before dipping it.""**"
"1111","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها narrated: > **""When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arose to perform ablution, he would tilt the vessel [to pour water over his hands], mention the Name of Allah Almighty (say Bismillāh), and then perform a complete and thorough ablution.""**"
"1112","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""O Abū Hurayrah, when you perform ablution, say: 'In the Name of Allah, and all praise is due to Allah' (Bismillāhi wal-ḥamdu lillāh); for indeed, your guardian angels will never cease recording good deeds for you until you break that ablution.""**"
"1113","Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq رضي الله عنه narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The tooth-stick (siwāk) is a purification for the mouth and a source of pleasure to the Lord.""**"
"1114","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Adhere to the tooth-stick, for it sweetens the mouth and brings pleasure to the Lord, Blessed and Exalted.""**"
"1115","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The tooth-stick is a purification for the mouth, a source of pleasure to the Lord, and a clarifier for the eyesight.""**"
"1116","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The tooth-stick is a purification for the mouth and a source of pleasure to the Lord.""**"
"1117","ʿAlī رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Were it not that I would place hardship upon my nation, I would have ordered them to use the tooth-stick with every ablution.""**"
"1118","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Were it not that I would place hardship upon my nation, I would have ordered them to perform ablution at every prayer, and to use the tooth-stick with every ablution.""**"
"1119","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Were it not that I would place hardship upon my nation, I would have ordered them to use the tooth-stick with ablution.""** Abū Hurayrah said: ""Indeed, I began using the tooth-stick before sleeping and after waking up, and before eating and after eating, ever since I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say what he said."""
"1120","Qutham ibn Tammām (or Tammām ibn Qutham) narrated from his father that he said: We came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: > **""Why do you come to me with discolored teeth (qulḥan)? Do you not use the tooth-stick? Were it not that I would place hardship upon my nation, I would have made the tooth-stick obligatory upon them just as I made ablution obligatory upon them.""**"
"1121","Tammām ibn al-ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Why do you enter upon me with discolored teeth? Use the tooth-stick! Were it not that I would place hardship upon my nation, I would have commanded them to use the tooth-stick at every purification.""**"
"1122","Al-ʿAbbās رضي الله عنه narrated: People used to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ without having cleaned their teeth with a tooth-stick, so he said: > **""You enter upon me with discolored teeth and do not use the tooth-stick! Were it not that I would place hardship upon my nation, I would have made the tooth-stick obligatory upon them just as I made ablution obligatory upon them.""** And ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها said: ""The Prophet ﷺ kept mentioning the tooth-stick so constantly that we feared Quranic revelation would descend regarding it."""
"1123","Abū Umāmah al-Bāhilī رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When one of you rinses his mouth, whatever sins he committed with his mouth are shed; when he washes his face, whatever he committed with his face is shed; when he washes his hands, whatever he committed with his hands is shed; when he wipes his head, his sins scatter from the roots of his hair; and when he washes his feet, whatever he committed with his feet is shed.""**"
"1124","Shahr ibn Ḥawshab narrated: Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه conveyed to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whichever man stands up for his ablution intending prayer, and then washes his palms, every sin falls from his palms with the very first drop. When he rinses his mouth, inhales water into his nose, and blows it out, every sin falls from his tongue and his lips with the first drop. When he washes his face, every sin falls from his hearing and his sight with the first drop. When he washes his arms to the elbows and his feet to the ankles, he is cleansed of every sin, just as he was on the day his mother gave birth to him. Then, if he stands for prayer, Allah elevates his rank; and if he sits, he sits safe [and cleansed of sin].""**"
"1125","Abū Muslim narrated: I entered upon Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه while he was in the mosque, and I said, ""O Abū Umāmah, a man narrated to me on your authority that you said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Whoever performs ablution and does so thoroughly—washing his hands and face, and wiping over his head and ears—then stands up for the obligatory prayer, Allah forgives him on that day for all that his feet walked towards, all that his hands grasped, all that his ears listened to, all that his eyes gazed upon, and whatever evil his inner self whispered.""**'"" Abū Umāmah said: ""By Allah, I heard it from the Prophet of Allah ﷺ more times than I can count!"""
"1126","Abū Ghālib narrated that he met Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه in Ḥimṣ and questioned him about various matters. Abū Umāmah related to them that he heard the Prophet ﷺ saying: > **""No Muslim servant hears the call to prayer and stands up for his ablution, except that he is forgiven with the very first drop of that water that touches his palm, and according to the number of those drops until he completes his ablution, except that all his past sins are forgiven, and he stands for his prayer while it is an extra reward (nāfilah) for him.""** Abū Ghālib said: I asked Abū Umāmah, ""Did you hear this directly from the Prophet ﷺ?"" He replied: ""Yes, by the One Who sent him with the truth as a bearer of glad tidings and a warner—not just once, nor twice, nor thrice, nor four times, nor five, nor six, nor seven, nor eight, nor nine, nor ten, nor twenty times!"" and he clapped his hands together."
"1127","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه also narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When the Muslim performs ablution and washes his hands, I expiate through it what his hands have committed; when he washes his face, I expiate from him what his eyes have looked upon; when he wipes his head, it expiates what his ears have heard; and when he washes his feet, I expiate from him what his feet have walked toward. Then he stands up for prayer, and it becomes an added virtue for him.""**"
"1128","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When a Muslim man performs ablution, his sins depart from his hearing, his sight, his hands, and his feet; and if he sits, he sits forgiven.""**"
"1129","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه narrated in a hadith traced directly to the Prophet ﷺ that he said: > **""No Muslim performs ablution, washing his hands, rinsing his mouth, and performing ablution as he was commanded, except that Allah sheds from him whatever sins he committed on that day—what his mouth uttered, what his hand touched, and what he walked toward—until his errors slide off from the extremities of his limbs. Then, when he walks to the mosque, one foot records a good deed while the other erases a bad deed.""**"
"1130","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When a Muslim performs ablution, sin departs from his hearing, his sight, his hands, and his feet.""** The narrator said: Then Abū Ṭaybah came while he was narrating this to us and asked, ""What is he narrating to you?"" So we mentioned to him what he had narrated to us. Thereupon, a man said: ""I heard ʿAmr ibn ʿAbasah narrate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,"" adding to it: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""No Muslim goes to sleep in a state of ritual purity, then awakens during the night and mentions Allah and asks Allah for any good from the good of this world and the Hereafter, except that Allah grants it to him.""**"
"1131","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه said: > **""When you apply the water of purification to its proper places, you sit down forgiven; and if you pray, it is an added virtue for you.""** A man asked, ""O Abū Umāmah, what do you think if he stands up and prays: is it considered a surplus voluntary deed (nāfilah) for him?"" He replied: ""No, a voluntary deed as a pure surplus was uniquely for the Prophet ﷺ. How could it be a surplus for an ordinary person when he constantly strives amidst sins and errors? Rather, it is an added virtue and a reward for him."""
"1132","A man from the people of Madinah narrated: The caller to prayer proclaimed the call for the ʿAṣr prayer. ʿUthmān رضي الله عنه called for water of purification, purified himself, and then said: ""I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: > **""Whoever performs ablution as he was commanded and prays as he was commanded, his sins are expiated from him.""**"" He then sought the testimony of four Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to confirm this, and they all bore witness to that on the authority of the Prophet ﷺ."
"1133","ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān رضي الله عنه called for water: he rinsed his mouth, inhaled water into his nose and expelled it, then washed his face three times, washed his arms three times, wiped his head and the tops of his feet, and then smiled and laughed. He said to his companions: ""Will you not ask me what made me laugh?"" They asked: ""What made you laugh, O Commander of the Faithful?"" He said: ""I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution just as I have performed ablution, then he smiled and laughed, saying: 'Will you not ask me what made me laugh?' They asked: 'What made you laugh, O Messenger of Allah?' He ﷺ replied: > **""Indeed, when the servant calls for ablution water and washes his face, Allah sheds from him every error he committed with his face; and when he washes his arms, it is likewise; when he wipes his head, it is likewise; and when he purifies his feet, it is likewise.""**"""
"1134","Thaʿlabah ibn ʿAbbād narrated from his father رضي الله عنه, who said: ""I do not know how many times the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated this to him, whether in pairs or odd numbers; he ﷺ said: > **""No servant performs ablution, perfecting his ablution, washing his face until water flows over his chin, then washing his arms until water flows over his elbows, then washing his feet until water flows from his ankles, and then stands up and prays, except that Allah forgives him all his past sins.""**"""
"1135","Abū ʿUshshānah al-Maʿāfirī reported that he heard ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir رضي الله عنه say: ""I shall not attribute anything to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ today that he did not say; I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""A man from my nation rises at night, wrestling with his soul to purify himself while knots are tied upon him. He performs ablution: when he washes his hands, a knot is untied; when he washes his face, a knot is untied; when he wipes his head, a knot is untied; and when he washes his feet, a knot is untied. Then the Lord, Mighty and Majestic, says to those beyond the veil: 'Look at this servant of Mine wrestling with his soul; whatever My servant asks of Me, it is his.'""**"""
"1136","Murrah ibn Kaʿb (or Kaʿb ibn Murrah) رضي الله عنه narrated: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, ""Which part of the night is most readily heard [for prayers to be answered]?"" He replied: ""The depth of the latter part of the night."" He then mentioned the narration until he said: > **""When the servant performs ablution and washes his hands, his errors tumble down from his hands; when he washes his face, his errors tumble down from his face; when he washes his arms, his errors tumble down from his arms; and when he washes his feet, his errors tumble down from his feet.""**"
"1137","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There is no one from my nation except that I will recognize him on the Day of Resurrection.""** They asked: ""O Messenger of Allah, both those you have seen and those you have not seen?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""Both those I have seen and those I have not seen: radiant with white blazes on their foreheads and luminous marks on their limbs from the traces of ablution (ghurran muḥajjalīn).""**"
"1138","Anas رضي الله عنه narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The likeness of my nation is that of a river in which one bathes five times a day: what dirt could possibly remain upon him? A person rises for ablution and washes his hands, and every error he touched with his hands scatters; he rinses his mouth, and every error his tongue uttered scatters; then he washes his face, and every error his eyes gazed upon scatters; then he wipes his head, and every error his ears listened to scatters; then he washes his feet, and every error his feet walked toward scatters.""**"
"1139","Anas رضي الله عنه narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, a righteous trait may exist in a man, and through it Allah sets right all of his deeds; and a man's purification for his prayer—Allah expiates his sins through his purification, and his prayer remains for him as a surplus reward (nāfilah).""**"
"1140","Abū al-Dardāʾ رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""I am the first to be granted permission to prostrate on the Day of Resurrection, and I am the first to raise his head. I will look before me and recognize my nation from among all nations, and likewise behind me, to my right, and to my left.""** A man asked: ""O Messenger of Allah, how will you recognize your nation from among all the nations from the time of Noah until your nation?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""They will have radiant white blazes on their foreheads and luminous marks on their limbs from the traces of ablution—a distinction belonging to no one besides them; I will recognize them by their records being given in their right hands; and I will recognize them by their offspring rushing before them.""**"
"1141","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه narrated: They asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, how will you recognize those you have not seen of your nation?"" He ﷺ said: > **""[They will be] radiant with white blazes on their foreheads and luminous marks on their limbs from ablution.""**"
"1142","Jābir رضي الله عنه narrated: It was said, ""O Messenger of Allah, how will you recognize those of your nation whom you have not seen?"" He ﷺ said: > **""[They will have] white blazes—"" and I believe he added: ""—and luminous marks on their limbs from the traces of ablution.""**"
"1143","ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir رضي الله عنه said: ""I arrived among twelve mounted men until we dismounted before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. My companions said, 'Who will tend to our camels while the rest of us go and learn from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when he returns, we will impart to him what we heard?' I said, 'I will.' Then I said to myself, 'Perhaps I am at a loss: shall my companions hear from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what I do not hear?' So one day I attended [his gathering], and I heard a man saying: The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever performs a complete ablution and then stands for prayer shall be freed from his sins just as he was on the day his mother gave birth to him.""**"
"1144","Abū Lubābah ibn ʿAbd al-Mundhir رضي الله عنه said: ""I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning purification (ablution), and he said: > **""No Muslim rinses his mouth except that Allah forgives him every sin committed by his tongue that day; nor does he wash his hands except that Allah forgives him whatever his hands committed that day; nor does he wipe his head except that he becomes [as free of sins] as on the day his mother gave birth to him.""**"
"1145","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""No Muslim performs ablution for prayer and rinses his mouth except that every misdeed spoken by his tongue departs with the drops of water; nor does he inhale water into his nose except that every misdeed whose scent he sensed with his nose departs with the drops of water; nor does he wash his face except that every misdeed he looked upon with his eyes scatters from his eyes with the drops of water; nor does he wash any part of his arms except that every misdeed struck by them departs with the drops of water; nor does he wash any part of his feet except that every misdeed he walked toward with them departs with the drops of water. Then, when he departs for the mosque, a good deed is recorded for him for every step he takes, and an evil deed is erased from him, until he arrives at his place of standing [for prayer].""**"
"1146","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whoever spends the night in a state of purity, an angel spends the night within his undergarment. He does not awaken at any hour of the night except that the angel supplicates: 'O Allah, forgive Your servant, as he spent the night in a state of purity.'""**"
"1147","Abū al-Janūb said: ""I saw ʿAlī [ibn Abī Ṭālib] رضي الله عنه drawing water for his ablution, so I hastened to draw it for him. He said: 'Refrain, O Abū al-Janūb! For indeed, I saw ʿUmar [ibn al-Khaṭṭāb] drawing water for his ablution, and I hastened to draw it for him. He said: 'Refrain, O Abū al-Ḥasan! For indeed, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drawing water for his ablution, and I hastened to draw it for him, whereupon he ﷺ said: > **""Refrain, O ʿUmar! Indeed, I dislike having anyone share with me in my purification.""**"
"1148","Abū Ayyūb رضي الله عنه said: > **""I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when the sun had set—or when it turned yellow nearing sunset—and I had with me a pitcher of water. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to relieve himself, and I sat waiting for him until he returned, and I helped him perform ablution...""** [The narrator mentioned the rest of the hadith.]"
"1149","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Allah does not accept charity from misappropriated spoils, nor prayer without purification.""**"
"1150","Al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""No prayer is accepted except with purification, and no charity from misappropriated spoils.""**"
"1151","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Allah does not accept charity from misappropriated spoils, nor prayer without purification.""**"
"1152","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: ""I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: > **""Allah does not accept a prayer without purification, nor charity from misappropriated spoils.""**"
"1153","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""No prayer is accepted without purification, nor charity from misappropriated spoils.""**"
"1154","ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Allah does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from misappropriated spoils.""**"
"1155","Abū Sabrah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There is no prayer for the one who has no ablution; there is no ablution for the one who does not mention the name of Allah upon it; he does not believe in Allah who does not believe in me; and he does not believe in me who does not recognize the right of the Anṣār.""**"
"1156","Abū al-Dardāʾ رضي الله عنه reported in a marfūʿ narration that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""There is no prayer for the one who has no ablution.""**"
"1157","ʿĪsā ibn Sabrah reported from his father, from his grandfather [Sabrah] رضي الله عنه, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit one day, praised and extolled Allah, and then said: > **""O people! There is no prayer except with ablution; there is no ablution for the one who does not mention the name of Allah upon it; he has not believed in Allah who has not believed in me; and he has not believed in me who does not recognize the right of the Anṣār.""**"
"1158","Rabāḥ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥuwayṭib narrated from his grandmother [Ruqayqah bint Abī Ṣayfī] رضي الله عنها, who said: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""He has not believed in Allah who has not believed in me; he has not believed in me who does not love the Anṣār; there is no prayer for the one who has no ablution; and there is no ablution for the one who does not mention the name of Allah upon it.""**"
"1159","Saʿd ibn ʿUmārah al-Bakrī رضي الله عنه—a companion of the Prophet ﷺ from Banū Saʿd ibn Bakr—was asked by a man: ""Admonish me concerning myself, may Allah have mercy on you."" He replied: > **""When you stand for prayer, perform ablution thoroughly; for indeed, there is no prayer for the one who has no ablution, and there is no faith for the one who has no prayer...""** [He then mentioned the rest of the hadith, which appears in the Book of Exhortations.]"
"1160","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: ""Shall I not inform you of the ablution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"" > **He called for water, and began scooping with his right hand and pouring it over his left hand.**"
"1161","ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān رضي الله عنه called for water and performed ablution near the stone benches (al-Maqāʿid), washing each limb three times. Then he asked the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: ""Did you see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do this?"" > **They said, ""Yes.""**"
"1162","Abū al-Naḍr reported that ʿUthmān [ibn ʿAffān] رضي الله عنه called for ablution water in the presence of al-Zubayr, Ṭalḥah, ʿAlī, and Saʿd رضي الله عنهم. He performed ablution while they watched: he washed his face three times, poured water over his right arm three times, and over his left arm three times; wiped his head; sprinkled water upon his right foot three times and then washed it; then sprinkled water upon his left foot and washed it three times. Then he said to those present: ""I adjure you by Allah, Mighty and Majestic: do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ablution just as I have now performed ablution?"" > **They said, ""Yes.""** [And he did that on account of something that had reached him.]"
"1163","Ḥumrān ibn Abān said: ""I saw ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān رضي الله عنه call for ablution water while at the gate of the mosque. He washed his hands, rinsed his mouth, and blew his nose. Then he washed his face three times, washed his arms up to the elbows three times, wiped his head and passed his hands over the exterior of his ears, then passed them over his beard, and then washed his feet up to the ankles three times. Then he stood and prayed two rakʿahs, after which he said: 'I have performed ablution for you just as I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution, and then I prayed two rakʿahs just as I saw him pray.' He said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said upon concluding his two rakʿahs: > **""Whoever performs ablution just as I have performed ablution, then prays two rakʿahs without allowing his mind to wander during them, shall be forgiven whatever [sins occurred] between them and his prayer of yesterday.""**"
"1164","ʿUthmān [ibn ʿAffān] رضي الله عنه called for ablution water: he rinsed his mouth, inhaled water into his nose, washed his face three times, washed his arms three times, wiped his head, and purified his feet. Then he laughed and said: ""Will you not ask me what made me laugh?"" We said: ""What made you laugh, O Commander of the Faithful?"" He said: ""I laughed because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for ablution water near this very spot. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution just as I have performed ablution, then he laughed just as I have laughed, and then he said: 'Will you not ask me what made me laugh?' We said: 'What made you laugh, O Prophet of Allah?' He ﷺ said: > **""What made me laugh is that whenever a servant performs ablution and washes his face, Allah removes from him every sin he committed with his face; and when he washes his arms, the same occurs; and when he wipes his head, the same occurs; and when he purifies his feet, the same occurs.""**"
"1165","ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd رضي الله عنه reported: > **""The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution: he washed his arms twice, his face three times, and wiped his head twice.""**"
"1166","Yazīd ibn al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib reported that his father [al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib] رضي الله عنه said: ""Gather together so that I may show you how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ablution and how he used to pray, for indeed I do not know how much longer my companionship with you will last."" So he gathered his children and family, called for ablution water, rinsed his mouth, blew his nose, and washed his face three times. He washed his right arm three times, and washed this one—meaning the left—three times. Then he wiped his head and his ears, both their exterior and interior; and he washed this foot—meaning the right—three times, and washed this foot—meaning the left—three times. Then he said: > **""In this manner, I have spared no effort in showing you how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ablution.""**"
"1167","ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Qurād رضي الله عنه said: ""I went out with the Prophet ﷺ on Hajj. I saw him go out to relieve himself, so I followed him with a leather water jug or cup. Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to relieve himself, he went far away. So I sat waiting for him along the path until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned. I said to him, 'O Messenger of Allah, here is ablution water.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ approached me, poured water over his hand and washed it, then inserted his hand, cupped it, and poured water over his arm once. Then he wiped his head, scooped water once in his hand, and struck the tops of his feet with it, sprinkling water with his hand upon the tops of his feet."" > **""Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to relieve himself, he would go far away.""**"
"1168","Abū Ayyūb رضي الله عنه reported: > **""Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution, he rinsed his mouth and wiped his beard with water from underneath it.""**"
"1169","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution: he rinsed his mouth three times, inhaled water into his nose three times, washed his face three times, washed his arms three times, wiped his head three times, and washed his feet three times.""**"
"1170","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution: he washed his palms three times, rinsed his mouth three times, inhaled water into his nose three times, washed his face three times, and washed his arms three times.""**"
"1171","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whoever performs ablution once for each limb, that is the obligatory duty of ablution without which it is invalid; whoever performs ablution twice receives a double portion of reward; and whoever performs ablution three times, that is my ablution and the ablution of the prophets before me.""**"
"1172","Rāshid Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥimmānī said: ""I saw Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه at al-Zāwiyah and said to him, 'Inform me about the ablution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—how was it? For it has reached me that you used to assist him in performing ablution.' He said, 'Yes.' Then he called for ablution water: a basin and a stone vessel were brought and set before him. He poured water over his hands and thoroughly washed his palms. Then he rinsed his mouth three times, inhaled water into his nose three times, and washed his face three times. Then he drew forth his right arm and washed it three times, then washed the left three times. Then he wiped his head once, passing his hands over his ears and wiping them, and then inserted both his palms together into the water..."" [The narrator mentioned the rest of the hadith.] > **""In this manner did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution.""**"
"1173","Ibrāhīm ibn Abī ʿAblah said: ""I asked Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه, 'How should I perform ablution?' He replied, 'You ask me how I perform ablution, yet you do not ask me how I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution?! I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution washing each limb three times, and he said: > **""With this has my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me.""**"
"1174","Buraydah رضي الله عنه said: ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for ablution water. He performed ablution washing each limb once, and said: > **""This is the ablution without which Allah does not accept prayer.""** Then he performed ablution washing each limb twice, and said: > **""This was the ablution of the nations before you.""** Then he performed ablution washing each limb three times, and said: > **""This is my ablution and the ablution of the prophets before me.""**"
"1175","Abū Rāfiʿ رضي الله عنه said: > **""I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution: he washed his face three times, washed his arms three times, wiped his head and ears, and washed his feet three times. And on another occasion, I saw him perform ablution washing each limb once.""**"
"1176","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما narrated: ""A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked, 'O Messenger of Allah, how is ablution performed?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for ablution water: he washed his right hand three times, then introduced his right hand into the vessel, rinsed his mouth and inhaled water into his nose three times, washed his face and his arms three times, wiped his head and the exterior of his ears along with his head, and then washed his feet three times. Then he said: > **""This is the ablution; whoever exceeds this has transgressed and done wrong.""**"
"1177","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: ""I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was purifying himself. Before him was a vessel containing approximately the measure of a mudd—if it exceeded, it was by very little, and if it fell short, it was by very little. He washed his hands, rinsed his mouth, and inhaled water into his nose three times each; washed his face three times and ran his wet fingers through his beard; washed his arms three times; wiped his head and his ears twice each; and washed his feet until he cleansed them thoroughly. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, is this how purification is done?' He ﷺ said: > **""Thus has my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me.""**"
"1178","Wāʾil ibn Ḥujar رضي الله عنه said: ""I was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a vessel containing water was brought to him. He poured water onto his right hand three times, then dipped his right hand into the vessel and poured water with it over his left hand three times. He then dipped his right hand, cupped a handful of water, and rinsed his mouth, inhaled water into his nose, and blew it out three times. Next, he placed both palms into the vessel, scooped water with them, and washed his face three times, ran his wet fingers through his beard, wiped the inner contours of his ears, and inserted his little fingers into the ear canals so that the water reached inside. He then wiped his neck and the underside of his beard with the surplus water from his face. He washed his right forearm three times extending beyond the elbow, and washed the left likewise beyond the elbow. He then wiped his head three times, wiped the exterior of his ears, and wiped his neck and the underside of his beard with the surplus water from his head. Then he washed his right foot three times, running water between its toes, extending the water beyond the ankle and up the shin; and did likewise with the left foot. Then he took a handful of water in his right hand and poured it over his head until it cascaded down the sides of his head, and said: > **""This is the completion of ablution.""** Then he entered his prayer place, the people aligned in rows behind him, and he looked to his right and to his left..."" [The narrator mentioned the rest of the hadith.]"
"1179","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما reported: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution washing each limb once, then stood and prayed.""**"
"1180","Abū Bakrah رضي الله عنه said: > **""I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution: he washed his hands three times, rinsed his mouth three times, inhaled water into his nose three times, washed his face three times, washed his arms up to the elbows, and wiped his head by moving his hands from front to back and from back to front. Then he washed his feet three times, ran his fingers between his toes, and interlaced his fingers through his beard.""**"
"1181","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""When one of you performs ablution, let him rinse his mouth three times, for sins depart from his face; and let him wash his hands three times, wipe his head three times, then insert his fingers into his ears, and then pour water over his feet three times.""**"
"1182","ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbbād ibn Yaḥyā ibn Khallād al-Zuraqī said: ""We entered upon ʿAbdullāh ibn Unays رضي الله عنه, and he said: 'Shall I not show you how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution and how he prayed?' We said: 'Yes, indeed.' So he washed his hands three times, wiped his head moving frontward and backward, touched his ears, and washed his feet three times. Then he took a garment, wrapped himself in it, and prayed. Then he said: > **""In this manner did I see my beloved, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, perform ablution and pray.""**"
"1183","Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh رضي الله عنهما said: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to Baqīʿ al-Gharqad; he performed ablution, washing his face and his arms, and wiped his head. Then he took water with his right hand, sprinkled it over his feet, and washed them.""**"
"1184","Muʿādh ibn Jabal رضي الله عنه said: > **""The Prophet of Allah ﷺ used to perform ablution washing each limb once, twice, and thrice—he practiced all of that.""**"
"1185","Abū Kāhil رضي الله عنه said: ""I passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was performing ablution. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Allah has granted us immense good through you.' He washed his palms, rinsed his mouth three times, inhaled water into his nose three times, washed his face three times, and washed his arms three times; he wiped his head without setting a specific number, and purified his feet without setting a specific number. Then he said: > **""O Abū Kāhil, apply the purification water to its proper places, and keep the surplus of your water for your household; do not leave your family thirsty, and do not burden your servant.""**"
"1186","Abū Ayyūb رضي الله عنه said: > **""Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution, he inhaled water into his nose three times, rinsed his mouth, and inserted his fingers into his mouth. When he washed his face, he reached with his palms to the front part of his ears; and when he wiped his head, he wiped with his fingers the rear part, and wiped his ears along with his head.""**"
"1187","ʿAbbād ibn Tamīm narrated from his father [Tamīm al-Māzinī] رضي الله عنه, who said: > **""I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performing ablution: he began by washing his face and his arms, then rinsed his mouth and inhaled water into his nose, and then wiped his head.""**"
"1188","Tamīm al-Māzinī رضي الله عنه said: > **""I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution and wipe with water over his beard and his feet.""**"
"1189","Nimrān ibn Jāriyah narrated from his father [Jāriyah ibn Ẓafar] رضي الله عنه that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Take fresh water for wiping the head.""**"
"1190","Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī رضي الله عنهما reported: > **""Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution, he would leave a surplus of water so that he poured it over the place of his prostration.""**"
"1191","Al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī رضي الله عنهما reported: > **""The Prophet ﷺ was performing ablution, and he washed the place of his prostration with water until he caused water to flow over the place of his prostration.""**"
"1192","ʿAbbād ibn Tamīm narrated from his father [Tamīm al-Māzinī] رضي الله عنه, who said: > **""I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution and wipe with water over his feet.""**"
"1193","ʿAbdullāh ibn Badr said: > **""The Quran was revealed mentioning wiping [the feet], but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to wash them, so we washed.""**"
"1194","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه reported regarding the verse: *""And [wash] your feet up to the ankles""* [al-Māʾidah 5:6]: > **""His verdict settled upon the washing of the two feet.""**"
"1195","ʿUthmān [ibn ʿAffān] رضي الله عنه said: ""Shall I not show you how the ablution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was?"" They replied: ""Yes, indeed."" So he called for water: he rinsed his mouth three times, blew water from his nose three times, washed his face three times, washed his arms three times, wiped his head, and washed his feet three times. Then he said: > **""Know that the two ears are part of the head.""** Then he said: ""I have meticulously reproduced for you the ablution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."""
"1196","Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The two ears are part of the head.""**"
"1197","ʿUmar ibn Abān ibn Mufaḍḍal al-Madanī said: ""Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه demonstrated ablution to me. He took a small jug and placed it on his left side, poured water upon his right hand and washed it three times, then turned the jug toward his right hand and washed it three times. He then wiped his head three times, took fresh water for his ear canals, and wiped them. I said: 'You have wiped your ears!' He said: 'O boy, indeed they are part of the head; they are not part of the face.' Then he asked: 'O boy, did you see? And did you understand, or shall I repeat it for you?' I said: 'It is sufficient for me, and I have understood.' He said: > **""In this manner did I see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution.""**"
"1198","Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī رضي الله عنه and ʿAṭāʾ reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""How excellent are those from my Ummah who run [water/toothpicks] between [their limbs and teeth] in ablution and after food!""**"
"1199","Abū Ayyūb [al-Anṣārī] رضي الله عنه said: ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and said: 'How excellent are those from my Ummah who clean between!' They asked: 'And who are those who clean between, O Messenger of Allah?' He ﷺ said: > **""Those who clean between in ablution and those who clean between after food. As for cleaning between in ablution, it is rinsing the mouth, inhaling water into the nose, and running water between the fingers and toes; and as for cleaning between after food, it is removing remnants of food. Indeed, nothing is more distressing to the two guardian angels than to see food between the teeth of their companion while he stands praying.""**"
"1200","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""How excellent are those from my Ummah who clean between [their digits in ablution and teeth after food]!""**"
"1201","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها reported: > **""Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution, he would run his wet fingers through his beard with water.""**"
"1202","Shaqīq said: ""ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān رضي الله عنه performed ablution and ran his wet fingers between his toes, and said: > **""I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do that.""**"
"1203","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها reported: > **""Whenever the Prophet ﷺ performed ablution, he would run his wet fingers through his beard.""**"
"1204","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported: > **""Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution, he would run his wet fingers through his beard.""**"
"1205","Abū al-Dardāʾ رضي الله عنه said: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution: he ran his wet fingers through his beard with the surplus water of his ablution, and wiped his head with the surplus water from his arms.""**"
"1206","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه said: ""I assisted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in performing ablution. He inserted his hand beneath his chin and ran his fingers through his beard. I asked: 'What is this?' He ﷺ said: > **""With this has my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me.""**"
"1207","Nāfiʿ reported from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما: > **""Whenever he performed ablution, he would run his wet fingers through his beard and between his toes, stating that he had seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ doing that.""**"
"1208","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUkbūrah رضي الله عنه—who was honored with companionship of the Prophet ﷺ—said: > **""Running the fingers through [the beard and between digits] is a Sunnah.""**"
"1209","Wāthilah [ibn al-Asqaʿ] رضي الله عنه narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whoever does not run water between his fingers and toes, Allah will run Fire between them on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"1210","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Either the fingers and toes must be thoroughly penetrated with purification water, or Fire shall surely penetrate them!""**"
"1211","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: > **""Run water between the five digits lest Allah stuff them with Fire.""**"
"1212","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Clean between your teeth and digits, for indeed it is cleanliness; cleanliness invites to faith, and faith accompanies its possessor in Paradise.""**"
"1213","ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""O ʿAlī, perform ablution thoroughly even when it is arduous for you, do not consume charity, do not mate donkeys with horses, and do not sit in the gatherings of astrologers.""**"
"1214","ʿAmr ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Kaʿb reported from a woman among those who had pledged allegiance [to the Prophet ﷺ] رضي الله عنها, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us accompanied by his companions from Banū Salimah. We presented food to him, and he and his companions ate. Then we brought him ablution water, and he performed ablution. He then turned toward his companions and said: 'Shall I not inform you of that which expiates sins?' They said: 'Yes, indeed.' He ﷺ said: > **""Performing ablution thoroughly despite hardships, taking many steps toward the mosques, and waiting for the next prayer after the prayer.""**"
"1215","ʿUbaydah ibn ʿAmr al-Kilābī رضي الله عنه said: > **""I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution, and he performed it thoroughly.""** [The narrator added: And Ribʿiyyah, whenever she performed ablution, would perform it thoroughly.]"
"1216","Ḥumrān said: ""ʿUthmān [ibn ʿAffān] رضي الله عنه called for ablution water as he intended to go out for prayer on a cold night. I brought him water, and he washed his face and his arms. I said: 'That is sufficient for you; the night is intensely cold!' But he said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""No servant performs ablution thoroughly except that Allah forgives him his past and future sins.""**"
"1217","ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whoever performs ablution thoroughly in severe cold shall have a double portion of reward.""**"
"1218","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, the angels rejoice at the departure of winter out of mercy for the hardship that befalls the poor among the believers.""**"
"1219","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to perform ablution thoroughly.""**"
"1220","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Shall I not guide you to that by which Allah expiates sins? Performing ablution thoroughly and taking many steps to the mosques.""**"
"1221","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked, ""What is the thorough performance of ablution?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent until the prayer was due. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water, washed his hands, expelled water from his nostrils, rinsed his mouth, washed his face three times, washed his arms three times each, wiped his head, and washed his feet three times each. Then he sprinkled water beneath his garment and said: > **""This is the thorough performance of ablution.""**"
"1222","Abū Rāfiʿ رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us with a radiant complexion, joy evident upon his face, and said: > **""I saw my Lord in the most magnificent form, and He said to me: 'O Muḥammad, do you know what the Exalted Assembly are disputing about?' I said: 'O my Lord, concerning the expiations.' He said: 'And what are the expiations?' I said: 'Performing ablution thoroughly reaching all its places despite hardships, walking on foot to the prayers, and waiting for the prayer after the prayer.'""**"
"1223","Ṭāriq ibn Shihāb رضي الله عنه reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked, ""Concerning what is the Exalted Assembly disputing?"" He replied: > **""Concerning the expiations and the elevated ranks. As for the elevated ranks, they are feeding others, spreading greetings of peace, and praying at night while the people are asleep. As for the expiations, they are performing ablution thoroughly during freezing cold mornings, walking to congregational prayers, and waiting for the prayer after the prayer.""**"
"1224","Khawlah bint Qays ibn Fahd رضي الله عنها narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Shall I not inform you of that which expiates sins?""** They said, ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah!"" He said: > **""Performing ablution thoroughly despite adversity, taking many steps to the mosques, and waiting for the prayer after the prayer.""**"
"1225","Saʿīd ibn Khaytham reported: I heard my grandmother ʿUbaydah bint ʿAmr al-Kilābiyyah رضي الله عنها say: > **""I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution, and he performed the ablution thoroughly.""**"
"1226","Wābiṣah ibn Maʿbad رضي الله عنه said: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about everything, until I even asked him about the dirt that accumulates beneath the fingernails. He ﷺ said: > **""Leave that which makes you doubt for that which does not make you doubt.""**"
"1227","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Why should I not be confused [in recitation] when the dirt of one of you is lodged between his fingertip and his nail?""**"
"1228","ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Baylamānī reported: I saw ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān رضي الله عنه sitting at the stone benches performing ablution. A man passed by him and greeted him with peace, but he did not return the greeting until he had finished his ablution. Then he entered the mosque, stood by the man, and said, ""Nothing prevented me from returning your greeting except that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **'Whoever performs ablution, washing his hands, then rinsing his mouth three times, sniffing water into his nostrils three times, washing his face three times, washing his arms up to the elbows, wiping his head, and then washing his feet, and thereafter does not speak until he says: ""I bear witness that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah alone, without partner, and that Muḥammad is His slave and His Messenger"" — he will be forgiven whatever occurred between the two ablutions.'""**"
"1229","Thawbān رضي الله عنه, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever calls for water for ablution, and the moment he finishes his ablution says: 'I bear witness that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, and I bear witness that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah; O Allah, make me among those who constantly repent, and make me among those who purify themselves' — the eight gates of Paradise will be opened for him, to enter through whichever of them he pleases.""**"
"1230","Muʿāwiyah ibn Qurrah reported from his father, from his grandfather [Iyās ibn Hilāl al-Muzanī رضي الله عنه], who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution washing each limb once and said: > **""This is an ablution without which Allah does not accept any prayer.""** Then he performed ablution washing each limb twice and said: > **""Whoever performs ablution like this, Allah will double his reward twice over.""** Then he performed ablution washing each limb three times and said: > **""This is the thorough performance of ablution, and this is my ablution and the ablution of the Close Friend of Allah, Abraham (Ibrāhīm) عليه السلام. Whoever performs ablution like this and then says: 'I bear witness that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah alone, without partner, and that Muḥammad is His slave and His Messenger' — the eight gates of Paradise will be opened for him, to enter through whichever of them he pleases.""**"
"1231","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever recites Sūrat al-Kahf, it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection from his dwelling to Makkah; and whoever recites the last ten verses of it, then if the Dajjāl emerges, he will not harm him; and whoever performs ablution and then says: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; there is no deity worthy of worship except You; I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You' — it will be inscribed upon a parchment, then set into a seal, never to be broken until the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"1232","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When one of you performs ablution for the prayer, let him not intertwine his fingers.""**"
"1233","Yazīd ibn Abī ʿUbayd reported: Whenever Salamah ibn al-Akwaʿ رضي الله عنه performed ablution, he would take musk, rub it into his hands, and then wipe his beard with it."
"1234","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever forgets to wipe the head and remembers while he is praying: if he finds moisture in his beard, let him take from it and wipe his head with it, for that will suffice him; but if he finds no moisture, let him repeat both the ablution and the prayer.""**"
"1235","Muʿayqīb رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Woe to the heels from the Fire!""**"
"1236","ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Jazʾ al-Zubaydī رضي الله عنه, one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Woe to the heels and the soles of the feet from the Fire!""**"
"1237","Abū Umāmah and his brother رضي الله عنهما reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw some people performing ablution, and upon their feet a spot the size of a dirham remained unwashed, so he said: > **""Woe to the heels from the Fire!""**"
"1238","Bakr ibn Sawādah reported: I heard Abū al-Haytham رضي الله عنه say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw me performing ablution, so he said: > **""[Mind] the sole of the foot, O Abū al-Haytham!""**"
"1239","Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq رضي الله عنه reported: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man came who had performed ablution, but there was a spot upon his foot that water had not reached. The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Go and complete your ablution.""** And the man did so."
"1240","Abū Rawḥ al-Kalāʿī رضي الله عنه reported: The Prophet of Allah ﷺ led us in a prayer in which he recited Sūrat al-Rūm, and a portion of it became confused for him. When he finished, he said: > **""Satan only confused the recitation for us because of certain people who come to the prayer without [proper] ablution. So whenever you come to the prayer, perform the ablution well.""**"
"1241","Shabīb Abū Rawḥ from Dhū al-Kalāʿ رضي الله عنه reported: He prayed alongside the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ recited Sūrat al-Rūm and hesitated at a verse. When he concluded the prayer, he said: > **""The recitation of the Qur'an was confused for us. Indeed, some people among you pray with us who do not perform ablution properly. So whoever attends the prayer with us, let him perform the ablution well.""**"
"1242","Rabīʿah al-Jurashī رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Remain steadfast, and excellent it is if you remain steadfast! Guard your ablution, for indeed the best of your deeds is prayer. And be mindful of the earth, for it is your mother; indeed, there is no one who performs upon it good or evil except that it will report it.""**"
"1243","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها narrated: > **""Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ emerged from relieving himself, he would perform ablution.""**"
"1244","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinated, and ʿUmar رضي الله عنه stood behind him holding a jug of water. The Prophet ﷺ asked, ""What is this, O ʿUmar?"" He replied, ""Water for you to perform ablution with, O Messenger of Allah."" He ﷺ said: > **""I have not been commanded to perform ablution every time I urinate; had I done so, it would have become an established sunnah.""**"
"1245","Usāmah ibn Zayd رضي الله عنهما narrated from the Prophet ﷺ: When Gabriel (Jibrīl) عليه السلام descended to the Prophet ﷺ, he taught him ablution. When Gabriel finished his ablution, he took a handful of water and sprinkled it toward his private parts: > **""And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to sprinkle water [over his private parts] after his ablution.""**"
"1246","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, when one of you is in prayer, Satan comes to him and urges him as a man urges his beast. If he yields to him, Satan produces a sound of passing wind between his buttocks to tempt him away from his prayer. Therefore, if anyone experiences anything of that sort, let him not leave [the prayer] until he hears a sound or detects an odor.""**"
"1247","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, when one of you is in the mosque, Satan comes to him and urges him as a man urges his beast. If he yields to him, he puts a tight tether on him or bridles him.""** Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said: ""And you see that: as for the tethered one, you see him leaning to one side; and as for the bridled one, you see him with his mouth agape, not remembering Allah."""
"1248","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported: The Prophet ﷺ was asked about a man who imagines during his prayer that he has broken his ritual purity when he has not. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, Satan comes to one of you while he is in his prayer and parts his buttocks so that it is imagined to him that he has broken his ritual purity when he has not. If any of you experiences that, let him not leave [the prayer] until he hears the sound of it with his ear or detects the odor of it with his nose.""**"
"1249","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, Satan comes to one of you while he is in his prayer and pulls a hair from his rear, so that he imagines he has broken his ablution. Let him not leave [the prayer] until he hears a sound or detects an odor.""**"
"1250","Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ reported: I saw al-Sāʾib ibn Khabbāb رضي الله عنه smelling his garment, so I said, ""Why are you doing that, may Allah have mercy upon you?"" He replied, ""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **'There is no ablution [required] except on account of an odor or hearing [a sound].'""**"
"1251","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: > **""Indeed, Satan comes to one of you during his prayer and tugs at a hair from his rear, causing him to think that he has broken his ablution. So let him not leave [his prayer] until he hears a sound or detects an odor.""**"
"1252","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: > **""Indeed, Satan circles around a man in his prayer to disrupt his prayer for him. When the man exhausts him, Satan blows into his rear. Therefore, if any of you senses anything of that sort, let him not leave [the prayer] until he detects an odor or hears a sound.""**"
"1253","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: > **""Ablution is required for that which exits, not for that which enters; and fasting is broken by that which enters, not by that which exits.""**"
"1254","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, reported: Salmā رضي الله عنها, the freed maidservant of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and wife of Abū Rāfiʿ رضي الله عنه, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ complaining about Abū Rāfiʿ because he had beaten her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked Abū Rāfiʿ, ""What is the matter between you and her, O Abū Rāfiʿ?"" He replied, ""She annoys me, O Messenger of Allah!"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked, ""In what way did you annoy him, O Salmā?"" She said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I did not annoy him with anything, but he passed wind while praying, so I said to him: 'O Abū Rāfiʿ, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has commanded the Muslims that whenever wind exits from one of them, he must perform ablution.' Thereupon he stood up and beat me!"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began to laugh and said: > **""O Abū Rāfiʿ, she only commanded you with good!""**"
"1255","Ḥuṣayn al-Muzanī reported: ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib رضي الله عنه said from the pulpit: ""O people, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **'Nothing invalidates the prayer except ritual impurity.'** I will not feel shy before you regarding that which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not feel shy about: ritual impurity is that one passes wind silently or audibly."""
"1256","ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib رضي الله عنه reported: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, we live in the desert, and a slight wind sometimes exits from one of us."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, Allah is not shy of the truth. When one of you does that, let him perform ablution; and do not approach women in their anuses.""**"
"1257","Jarīr ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Bajalī رضي الله عنه reported: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه was leading the people in prayer when something escaped from a person. ʿUmar said, ""I firmly resolve upon the one responsible for this that he perform ablution and repeat the prayer."" Jarīr said, ""What if you resolve upon everyone who heard it to perform ablution and repeat the prayer?"" ʿUmar said: > **""How excellent is what you have said! May Allah reward you with good.""** And he commanded all of them to do that."
"1258","Sayf ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥimyari reported: I entered along with some men upon ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها, and we asked her about a man who touches his private part. She said: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **'I do not care whether I touch it or touch my nose.'""**"
"1259","ʿIṣmah ibn Mālik al-Khaṭmī رضي الله عنه reported: A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, ""A part of my body itched, so I reached inside to scratch, and my hand touched my private part."" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""That happens to me as well.""**"
"1260","Arqam ibn Shuraḥbīl reported: I scratched my body while I was in prayer, and my hand came in contact with my private part. I mentioned this to ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه, and he said to me while laughing: > **""Cut it off then! How can you detach it from yourself? It is merely a piece of your flesh.""**"
"1261","ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAlqamah reported: Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه was asked while I was listening about touching the private part. He said: > **""Is it anything other than like the tip of your nose?""**"
"1262","Saʿīd ibn Jubayr reported that ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: > **""I do not care whether I touch it or touch the tip of my nose.""**"
"1263","Al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī reported: Five of the Companions of Muḥammad ﷺ — ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān, ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, and another man [رضي الله عنهم] — stated their view: one said, ""I do not care whether I touch my private part or the tip of my nose""; another said, ""My thigh""; and another said, ""My knee."""
"1264","Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī رضي الله عنه narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Whoever touches his private part, let him perform ablution.""**"
"1265","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whoever brings his hand in direct contact with his private part without any barrier between them, ablution has become obligatory upon him.""**"
"1266","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever touches his private part, let him perform ablution; and whichever woman touches her private part, let her perform ablution.""**"
"1267","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما reported: Busrah bint Ṣafwān رضي الله عنها asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a woman who inserts her hand into her private part. He ﷺ said: > **""Ablution is incumbent upon her.""**"
"1268","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whoever touches his private part, let him perform ablution.""**"
"1269","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whoever touches his private part, let him perform ablution.""**"
"1270","Ṭalq ibn ʿAlī رضي الله عنه — who was among the delegation that came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever touches his private part, let him perform ablution.""**"
"1271","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما reported: Busrah bint Ṣafwān ibn Nawfal رضي الله عنها asked the Prophet ﷺ about a woman whose hand strikes against her private part. He ﷺ said: > **""She must perform ablution.""**"
"1272","Busrah bint Ṣafwān رضي الله عنها reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Whoever touches his penis, his testicles, or his groins, let him perform ablution like his ablution for prayer.""**"
"1273","Buraydah ibn al-Ḥuṣayb رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever touches an idol, let him perform ablution.""**"
"1274","Al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām رضي الله عنه reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ met Gabriel عليه السلام and extended his hand to him, but Gabriel declined to take it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water and performed ablution, then extended his hand to him again, and Gabriel took it. The Prophet ﷺ asked: ""O Gabriel, what prevented you from taking my hand?"" Gabriel replied: > **""You had taken the hand of a Jewish man, and I disliked that my hand should touch a hand that had touched a disbeliever.""**"
"1275","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: > **""We used to perform ablution after touching a person afflicted with leprosy.""**"
"1276","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When one of you suffers a nosebleed in his prayer, let him depart, wash the blood off himself, repeat his ablution, and face the prayer anew.""**"
"1277","Salmān al-Fārisī رضي الله عنه reported: Blood flowed from my nose, so I asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: > **""Renew your ablution on account of what has occurred.""**"
"1278","Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī رضي الله عنه reported: While the Prophet ﷺ was leading the people in prayer, a visually impaired man entered and fell into a pit that was in the mosque. Many of the people laughed while they were in prayer. Thereupon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded: > **""Whoever laughed must repeat the ablution and repeat the prayer.""**"
"1279","Abū Masʿūd al-Anṣārī رضي الله عنه reported: A man set out for the prayer, and his wife met him on the way, so he embraced her and held her. He then came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him: > **""And he ﷺ did not forbid him [from praying without repeating his ablution].""**"
"1280","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها narrated: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would kiss [his wife], then go out to prayer and not renew his ablution.""**"
"1281","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها narrated: > **""The Prophet ﷺ would kiss some of his wives, then go out to prayer and not perform ablution.""**"
"1282","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: > **""Touching (al-mulāmasah) refers to what is short of sexual intercourse; if a man touches his wife's body with desire, ablution is obligatory upon him.""**"
"1283","Abū ʿUbaydah reported that ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: > **""A man must perform ablution on account of intimate skin contact, touching with his hand, and kissing when he kisses his wife.""** And regarding the verse: {or you have touched women} [al-Nisāʾ: 43], he used to say, ""It refers to squeezing/touching (al-ghamz)."""
"1284","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I suffer from hemorrhoids and discharge continuously flows from me."" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Once you have performed ablution, even if it flows from the crown of your head to your feet, no [further] ablution is incumbent upon you.""**"
"1285","Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī Sufyān رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, the two eyes are the drawstring of the anus; when the two eyes sleep, the drawstring is loosened.""**"
"1286","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""There is no ablution due upon one who falls asleep while prostrating until he lies down, for when he lies down, his joints become relaxed.""**"
"1287","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever falls asleep while sitting, there is no ablution due upon him; but when he lays his side down, ablution is incumbent upon him.""**"
"1288","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported: The Prophet ﷺ slept until he breathed deeply (snored), and then he said: > **""Ablution is only due upon the one who lies down.""**"
"1289","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported: > **""The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would lay down on their sides; then some of them would perform ablution, while others would not.""**"
"1290","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported from a number of people among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ: > **""They would lay down on their sides and fall asleep; then some of them would perform ablution, while others would not.""**"
"1291","ʿAbd al-Karīm Abū Umayyah reported that ʿAlī, Ibn Masʿūd, and al-Shaʿbī [رضي الله عنهم / رحمهم الله] said regarding a man who falls asleep while sitting: > **""There is no ablution due upon him.""**"
"1292","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The ablution of one overcome by drowsiness is that you touch water, and then with that touch you wipe your face, your arms, and your feet, like the wiping of dry ablution (tayammum).""**"
"1293","Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Perform ablution from that whose color has been altered by fire.""**"
"1294","Al-Qāsim, the freed slave of Muʿāwiyah, narrated: I entered the Mosque of Damascus and saw a group of people gathered around an elder who was narrating hadiths to them. I asked, ""Who is this?"" They replied, ""Sahl ibn al-Ḥanẓaliyyah رضي الله عنه."" Then I heard him say: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say:"" > **""Whoever eats meat, let him perform ablution.""**"
"1295","Muḥammad ibn Ṭaḥlāʾ narrated: I said to Abū Sulaymān, ""Indeed, your foster-relative Sulaym does not perform ablution after eating that which fire has touched."" Thereupon, Abū Sulaymān struck Sulaym on his chest and said, ""I bear witness concerning Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that she reported:"" > **""The Prophet ﷺ used to perform ablution after eating that which fire had touched.""**"
"1296","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Perform ablution from that which fire has altered.""**"
"1297","It is narrated that Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه placed his fingers upon his ears and said: ""May these ears become deaf if I did not hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say:"" > **""Perform ablution from that which fire has touched.""**"
"1298","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whoever touches his private parts, let him perform ablution."" And he ﷺ also said: ""Perform ablution from that which fire has altered.""**"
"1299","ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ghanm al-Ashʿarī reported: I asked Muʿādh ibn Jabal رضي الله عنه, ""Did you use to perform ablution from that which fire has altered?"" He replied: > **""Yes. When one of us ate something altered by fire, he would wash his hands and his mouth, and we used to consider that to be ablution (wuḍūʾ).""**"
"1300","ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Ablution is due from that which fire has touched.""**"
"1301","Abū Saʿd al-Khayr رضي الله عنه said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Perform ablution from that which fire has touched and which has boiled in cooking pots.""**"
"1302","Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī رضي الله عنه reported: > **""Whenever the Prophet ﷺ ate that which fire had altered, he would perform ablution.""**"
"1303","Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Perform ablution from that which fire has touched.""**"
"1304","Jubayrah ibn Maḥmūd reported that he and Salamah ibn Salāmah ibn Waqsh رضي الله عنه, a Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, entered a wedding feast while Salamah was already in a state of ablution. They ate and then went out, whereupon Salamah began to perform ablution again. Jubayrah asked him, ""Were you not already in a state of ablution?"" He replied, ""Yes, but indeed I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when we came out of an invitation to which we had been invited; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in a state of ablution, yet he ate and then performed ablution. I asked him, 'Were you not already in a state of ablution, O Messenger of Allah?' He ﷺ replied:"" > **""Yes, but new matters arise, and this is among what has newly arisen.""**"
"1305","ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Umāmah al-Balawī narrated from his father, Iyās ibn Thaʿlabah رضي الله عنه, who was a Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he said: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to perform ablution (i.e. wash) from the greasy residue of food (al-ghamr), so that we do not cause discomfort to one another.""**"
"1306","Dhū al-Ghurrah (Yaʿīsh al-Juhanī) رضي الله عنه reported: A Bedouin approached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was traveling and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, prayer overtakes us while we are in the resting pens of camels; may we pray in them?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied, **""No.""** He asked, ""Should we perform ablution after eating their meat?"" He ﷺ replied, **""Yes.""** He asked, ""May we pray in sheepfolds?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied, **""Yes.""** He asked, ""Should we perform ablution after eating their meat?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: > **""No.""**"
"1307","A freed slave or a son of Mūsā ibn Ṭalḥah reported from his father, from his grandfather [Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydillāh] رضي الله عنه, who said: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ablution after consuming the milk and meat of camels, but he would not perform ablution after consuming the milk and meat of sheep, and he would pray in sheepfolds.""**"
"1308","Usayd ibn Ḥuḍayr رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Perform ablution from the meat of camels, and do not pray in the resting places of camels. But do not perform ablution from the meat of sheep, and pray in sheepfolds.""**"
"1309","Samurah al-Suwāʾī رضي الله عنه said: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying, ""We are people of the desert and owners of livestock; should we perform ablution after consuming camel meat and its milk?"" He ﷺ replied, **""Yes.""** I asked, ""Should we perform ablution after consuming sheep meat and its milk?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""No.""**"
"1310","Sulayk al-Ghaṭafānī رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Perform ablution from the meat of camels, and do not perform ablution from the meat of sheep. Pray in sheepfolds, and do not pray in the resting places of camels.""**"
"1311","Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh رضي الله عنه reported: > **""The Prophet ﷺ drank some milk and then rinsed his mouth on account of its greasiness (fatness).""**"
"1312","ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān رضي الله عنه sat by the second door of the Mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and called for a shoulder of meat, from which he stripped meat with his teeth. Then he stood up and prayed without performing ablution, after which he said: > **""I have sat where the Prophet ﷺ sat, I have eaten what the Prophet ﷺ ate, and I have done what the Prophet ﷺ did.""**"
"1313","ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān رضي الله عنه reported: > **""He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eat bread and meat, and then pray without performing ablution.""**"
"1314","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه reported: > **""The Prophet ﷺ used to eat meat and then stand up for prayer without touching water (i.e. without repeating ablution).""**"
"1315","Al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah رضي الله عنه reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate some food, and then the prayer was called. He stood up, having already performed ablution prior to that. I brought him water so that he might perform ablution from it, but he rebuked me and said, **""Stay back!""** By Allah, that distressed me. He then prayed. I later mentioned that to ʿUmar رضي الله عنه, so ʿUmar said, ""O Prophet of Allah, al-Mughīrah was deeply distressed by your rebuking him, and he feared that you held something against him."" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""I hold nothing in my heart toward him except good. However, he brought me water to perform ablution when I had merely eaten food; had I done so, the people would have followed suit after me.""**"
"1316","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه said: My mother [Umm Sulaym], Abū Ṭalḥah, and I were sitting together and ate meat and bread. Then I called for water for ablution, whereupon they both asked, ""Why should we perform ablution?"" I replied, ""On account of this food that we have eaten."" They said: > **""Should we perform ablution on account of wholesome things? The one who is better than you (the Prophet ﷺ) did not perform ablution from it.""**"
"1317","Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq رضي الله عنه said: > **""The Prophet ﷺ bit off meat from a shoulder, and then prayed without performing ablution.""**"
"1318","ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib رضي الله عنه said: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to eat tharīd (meat-and-bread broth) and drink milk, and then pray without performing ablution.""**"
"1319","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said: > **""I scooped out a shoulder of meat for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the cooking pot of al-ʿAbbās; he ate it and then stood up to pray without performing ablution.""**"
"1320","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution after eating pieces of dried curd (aqiṭ), but later he ate a shoulder of mutton and then prayed without performing ablution.""**"
"1321","Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī Sufyān رضي الله عنه reported: > **""He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ consume milk, and then pray without performing ablution.""**"
"1322","Abū Umāmah al-Bāhilī رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ used to say to his Companions: > **""When one of you is in a state of ablution and eats food, he does not need to perform ablution on account of it, unless it is camel's milk; when you drink it, rinse your mouth with water.""**"
"1323","Abū Umāmah al-Bāhilī رضي الله عنه said: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not perform ablution from that which fire had touched.""**"
"1324","Abū Umāmah al-Bāhilī رضي الله عنه reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Ṣafiyyah bint ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib رضي الله عنها, and she served—or brought near to him—a piece of meat on the bone, placing it before him. Then she served—or brought near—another piece and placed it before him, and he ate. Then the muʾadhdhin came and called out, ""Ablution! Ablution!"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Ablution is only incumbent upon us on account of that which exits, and it is not incumbent upon us on account of that which enters.""**"
"1325","Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj رضي الله عنه said: > **""I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eat an arm of meat. When he finished, he wiped his fingers against the wall, then prayed ʿAṣr and Maghrib without performing ablution.""**"
"1326","Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī رضي الله عنهما reported: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by him while he had a bone with meat in his hand from which he was stripping meat. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it, bit off a morsel or two from it, and then prayed without performing ablution.""**"
"1327","Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī رضي الله عنهما reported: He entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the house of Fāṭimah رضي الله عنها. She handed the Prophet ﷺ a cooked shoulder of mutton and he ate it. Then he stood up to pray, whereupon she held onto his garment and said, ""Will you not perform ablution, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said, ""From what, my dear daughter?"" She replied, ""You have eaten that which fire has touched."" He ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, the purest of your food is that which fire has touched.""**"
"1328","Muḥammad ibn Maslamah رضي الله عنه reported: > **""The latter of the two practices of the Prophet ﷺ was that he ate meat and then prayed without performing ablution.""**"
"1329","Muʿādh ibn Jabal رضي الله عنه said: > **""The Prophet ﷺ only commanded ablution from that which fire has altered in the sense of washing the two hands and the mouth for the purpose of cleanliness, and it is not obligatory.""**"
"1330","Muʿādh ibn Jabal رضي الله عنه said: The Prophet ﷺ passed by me while I was skinning a sheep. He said to me, **""O Muʿādh, give it to me""**—or **""show me.""** He inserted his hand between the flesh and the hide once or twice [to separate the skin], and then said: > **""O Muʿādh, do it like this."" Then he proceeded to the prayer.**"
"1331","Sayyidah Fāṭimah رضي الله عنها narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited me and ate meat from a bone. Then Bilāl came with the call to prayer, so the Prophet ﷺ stood up to pray. I took hold of his garment and asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, will you not perform ablution?"" He asked, ""From what should I perform ablution, my dear daughter?"" I said, ""From that which fire has touched."" He ﷺ said: > **""Is not the finest (or purest) of your food that which fire has touched?""**"
"1332","Sayyidah ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها said: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would pass by the cooking pot, take a bone with meat and eat from it, and then pray without performing ablution and without touching water.""**"
"1333","Sayyidah Ṣafiyyah bint Ḥuyayy رضي الله عنها said: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me, so I presented to him a cold shoulder of meat which I had prepared and sliced. He ate it, and then stood up and prayed [without performing ablution].""**"
"1334","Sayyidah Ḍubāʿah bint al-Zubayr رضي الله عنها reported: > **""She presented meat to the Prophet ﷺ; he bit off some of it and then prayed without performing ablution.""**"
"1335","ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Nawfal reported that Umm Ḥakīm bint al-Zubayr رضي الله عنها narrated to him: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Ḍubāʿah رضي الله عنها and bit off meat from a shoulder in her presence, and then prayed without performing ablution on account of that.""**"
"1336","Sayyidah Umm Ḥakīm bint al-Zubayr رضي الله عنها said: > **""I handed the Prophet of Allah ﷺ a shoulder of meat; he ate from it and then prayed [without repeating ablution].""**"
"1337","Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir reported from Sayyidah Umm Hāniʾ رضي الله عنها: > **""He ate a shoulder of meat, and then prayed without performing ablution—referring to the Prophet ﷺ.""**"
"1338","Sayyidah Umm Mubashshir رضي الله عنها reported: > **""The Prophet ﷺ bit off meat from a shoulder, and then prayed without performing ablution.""**"
"1339","Sayyidah Umm Ḥakīm bint al-Zubayr رضي الله عنها used to prepare food for the Prophet ﷺ and send it to him, and sometimes he would visit her and eat in her home. She related that he came to her one day, so she brought him a shoulder of meat and sliced it for him. She stated: > **""He ate, and then prayed without performing ablution.""**"
"1340","Sayyidah ʿAmrah bint Ḥizām رضي الله عنها reported that she prepared a resting place for the Prophet ﷺ in a date-palm grove, sweeping and perfuming it. She slaughtered a sheep for him and he ate from it, then performed ablution and prayed Ẓuhr. Afterward, she presented more of its meat to him, which he ate, and then: > **""He prayed ʿAṣr without performing ablution anew.""**"
"1341","Hind bint Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī reported from her paternal aunt, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to visit Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه during his illness. We presented an arm of mutton to him, and he ate from it. When the prayer time arrived: > **""He rinsed his mouth, and then prayed without performing ablution.""**"
"1342","Sayyidah Umm Sulaym رضي الله عنها said: > **""I served a roasted shoulder of meat to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; he ate from it, then stood up for prayer without performing ablution.""**"
"1343","Sayyidah Umm ʿĀmir bint Yazīd ibn al-Sakan رضي الله عنها—who was among the women who pledged allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ—reported: > **""She brought the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a bone with meat on it, and he stripped the meat with his teeth while he was in the mosque of Banū ʿAbd al-Ashhal. Then he stood up and prayed without performing ablution.""**"
"1344","ʿAlqamah reported: We brought a large bowl of food containing bread and meat while we were with Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه. He ordered that it be placed in the pathway, and he ate from it and we ate along with him, while he invited everyone who passed by to join. Then we proceeded to the prayer, and: > **""He did nothing more than wash the tips of his fingers and rinse his mouth, then he prayed.""**"
"1345","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: > **""That I should perform ablution on account of a foul word is more beloved to me than performing ablution on account of wholesome food.""**"
"1346","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, **""Assist me with ablution.""** So I brought him water for ablution. He cleansed himself after relieving himself (istinjāʾ), then rubbed his hand in the dirt, wiped it, and washed it. He then performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks (khuffayn). I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, you did not wash your feet!"" He ﷺ replied: > **""Indeed, I put them into the leather socks while both feet were in a state of purity.""**"
"1347","Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī رضي الله عنه took off his leather socks, and the people began looking at him in surprise. Thereupon he said: > **""As for me, I have certainly seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wipe over them, but the full washing of ablution has been made beloved to me.""**"
"1348","Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī رضي الله عنه used to instruct people to wipe over their leather socks, yet he would wash his own feet. When he was asked about this, he said: > **""Wretched indeed would be my lot if the ease of it were for you while its sin fell upon me!""**"
"1349","Al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah رضي الله عنه said: I assisted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in performing ablution during a journey. He washed his face and his arms, wiped his head, and wiped over his leather socks. I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, shall I remove your leather socks?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""No, for I put them in while they were in a state of purity, and I have not walked barefoot since.""**"
"1350","Thawbān رضي الله عنه said: > **""I saw the Prophet ﷺ perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks (khuffayn) and head covering (khimār).""**"
"1351","Abū Barzah al-Aslamī رضي الله عنه mentioned in a lengthy hadith concerning the Prophet ﷺ: > **""The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks.""**"
"1352","ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه said: > **""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanding to wipe over the leather socks when one has put them on while the feet were in a state of purity.""**"
"1353","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه entered the privy, and when he came out, he wiped over his leather socks and said: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered [the privy], then came out and wiped over them both.""**"
"1354","ʿAwsajah narrated from his father رضي الله عنه, who said: > **""I traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he used to wipe over his leather socks.""**"
"1355","Maʿqil ibn Yasār رضي الله عنه reported: We were in the company of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah entered wearing leather socks. Al-Mughīrah was the first person in Islam whom I saw wearing leather socks. People began touching them and asking, ""What are these?"" He replied, ""Leather socks (khifāf)."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, leather socks will soon become abundant among you.""** They asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, what do you command us regarding ablution for prayer?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""Wipe over them""—or ""perform ablution over them.""**"
"1356","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه said: > **""I assisted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in performing ablution one month before his passing, and he wiped over his leather socks and turban.""**"
"1357","Abū Ṭalḥah al-Anṣārī رضي الله عنه reported: > **""The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks and head cloth (khimār).""**"
"1358","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه said: We went on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and arrived at a pool of water. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dismounted, and so did we. When the time for prayer arrived, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, **""O Bilāl, stand and call the adhān.""** Bilāl went and relieved himself, then came to the pool of water, washed his face and his hands, and was about to reach down to remove his leather socks—he was wearing two black leather socks—all while under the watchful gaze of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called out to him: > **""O Bilāl, wipe over the leather socks and the head covering!""**"
"1359","Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh رضي الله عنه said: The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man performing ablution who was washing his leather socks. The Prophet ﷺ prodded him with his foot and said: > **""The Sunnah is not like this. We were commanded to wipe over the leather socks like this."" And he passed his hands over his leather socks.**"
"1360","Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh رضي الله عنهما reported: > **""The Prophet ﷺ wiped over his leather socks.""**"
"1361","Jābir ibn Samurah رضي الله عنه reported: > **""The Prophet ﷺ wiped over his leather socks.""**"
"1362","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said: > **""I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution, wiping over his turban and wiping over his leather socks.""**"
"1363","Khuzaymah ibn Thābit رضي الله عنه reported: > **""The Prophet ﷺ used to wipe over his leather socks and head covering.""**"
"1364","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported: Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ and ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهم mentioned wiping over leather socks in the presence of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه. ʿUmar said to Ibn ʿUmar, ""Saʿd is more knowledgeable in jurisprudence than you."" Thereupon, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās said: > **""O Saʿd, we do not deny that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped [over leather socks], but did he wipe after Sūrat al-Māʾidah was revealed? For indeed it made everything decisive and was the last sūrah revealed in the Qur'an."" The narrator noted that no one spoke thereafter.**"
"1365","Usāmah ibn Zayd رضي الله عنهما reported: > **""The Prophet ﷺ wiped over his leather socks.""**"
"1366","ʿAwsajah ibn Muslim reported from his father رضي الله عنه, who said: > **""I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinate, then perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks.""**"
"1367","Abū Umāmah al-Bāhilī رضي الله عنه reported: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped over his leather socks and turban during the Expedition of Tabūk.""**"
"1368","Al-Sharīd رضي الله عنه reported: > **""The Prophet ﷺ wiped over his leather socks (khuffayn).""**"
"1369","Rabīʿah ibn Kaʿb al-Aslamī رضي الله عنه said: > **""I saw the Prophet ﷺ wiping over his leather socks.""**"
"1370","Abū Ayyūb رضي الله عنه said: > **""I saw the Prophet ﷺ wiping over the leather socks and the head-covering (khimār).""**"
"1371","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: > **""Whoever turns away from wiping over the leather socks has turned away from the Sunnah of Muḥammad ﷺ.""**"
"1372","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ continued to wipe over the leather socks until Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, took his soul.""**"
"1373","ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥasanah رضي الله عنه said: > **""I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks.""**"
"1374","ʿAbdullāh ibn Rawāḥah and Usāmah ibn Zayd رضي الله عنهم reported: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks.""**"
"1375","ʿIṣmah رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us in one of the alleyways of Medina and reached the refuse dump of a people. He said: > **""O Ḥudhayfah, screen me.""** The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then stood and urinated while standing, after which he called for water, performed ablution, wiped over his leather socks, and prayed."
"1376","ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ṭufayl said: I saw ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm رضي الله عنه wiping over the leather socks, and he said: > **""I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over his leather socks.""**"
"1377","Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib رضي الله عنه reported: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never ceased wiping over the leather socks both before the revelation of Sūrat al-Māʾidah and after it, until Allah took his soul.""**"
"1378","ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit رضي الله عنه said: > **""I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinate, then perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks.""**"
"1379","ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit رضي الله عنه reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a man who performs ablution thoroughly and wipes over his leather socks, yet whenever he wishes to pray, he removes them and performs ablution anew. He ﷺ replied: > **""No; rather, he should wipe over them.""**"
"1380","Abū Barzah رضي الله عنه said: > **""We were informed of a concession from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding wiping over the leather socks.""**"
"1381","It was reported concerning ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه: > **""He used to wipe over his stockings (jawrabayn) and sandals (naʿlayn).""**"
"1382","Yarīm ibn Asʿad said: I was with Qays ibn Saʿd رضي الله عنه—who had served the Prophet ﷺ for ten years—when he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks: > **""I have never forgotten the trace of his fingers upon the leather socks, for they were brand new.""**"
"1383","Hārūn ibn Sulaymān said: > **""I saw ʿAmr ibn Ḥurayth pass urine, then call for water; he washed his face and arms, wiped over his sandals, and then stood and prayed.""**"
"1384","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding wiping over the leather socks: > **""For the resident, it is one day and one night; and for the traveler, it is three days and their nights.""**"
"1385","ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār said: I asked Maymūnah رضي الله عنها, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, about wiping over the leather socks. She said: I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, may a person wipe over the leather socks at all times without taking them off?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""Yes.""**"
"1386","Maymūnah رضي الله عنها narrated that she asked: ""O Messenger of Allah, should a person take off his leather socks at every hour?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""No, but rather he may wipe over them as long as he wishes.""**"
"1387","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Regarding wiping over the leather socks: for the traveler, it is three days; and for the resident, one day and one night.""**"
"1388","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: > **""We used to wipe over the leather socks along with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: for the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident one day and one night.""**"
"1389","Abū ʿUbaydah ibn ʿAbdillāh said that Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه used to say: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us, when we were with him on a journey, not to remove our leather socks for three days and their nights, except on account of major ritual impurity (janābah); but not on account of urination or sleep.""**"
"1390","ʿAwf ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه said: > **""During the Expedition of Tabūk, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to wipe over the leather socks: three days and their nights for the traveler, and one day and one night for the resident.""**"
"1391","Jarīr رضي الله عنه said: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about wiping over the leather socks, and he replied: > **""Three days for the traveler, and one day and one night for the resident.""**"
"1392","Al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah رضي الله عنه said: I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he went to relieve himself. He gestured to me, so I went and brought him water. He was wearing a Syrian cloak without sleeves, so he cast it over his shoulders and said: > **""Pour water for me.""** So I poured water for him; he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks. Thus it became an established Sunnah: three days and their nights for the traveler, and one day and one night for the resident."
"1393","Al-Barāʾ رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""For the traveler, it is three days and their nights; and for the resident, one day and one night regarding wiping over the leather socks.""**"
"1394","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported from the Prophet ﷺ concerning wiping over the leather socks: > **""Three days for the traveler, and one day and one night for the resident.""**"
"1395","Abū Burdah رضي الله عنه said: > **""In the last military expedition we fought alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he commanded us to wipe over our leather socks: three days and their nights for the traveler, and one day and one night for the resident, as long as one does not remove them.""**"
"1396","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Wiping over the leather socks is one day and one night for the resident, and three days and their nights for the traveler.""**"
"1397","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported: > **""The Prophet ﷺ used to wipe over the leather socks and the turban for three days during travel, and for one day and one night while resident.""**"
"1398","Usāmah ibn Sharīk رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said concerning wiping over the leather socks: > **""For the traveler, three days; and for the resident, one day and one night.""**"
"1399","Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""For the traveler, three days and their nights; and for the resident, one day and one night regarding wiping over the leather socks.""**"
"1400","Khuzaymah ibn Thābit رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""For the traveler, three days and their nights; and for the resident, one day and one night. He may wipe over his leather socks provided that he put his feet into them while both were in a state of ritual purity.""**"
"1401","Yaʿlā ibn Murrah رضي الله عنه said: > **""Whenever we traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we would not remove our leather socks for three days; and when we were resident, for one day and one night.""**"
"1402","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: ""For the traveler, three days and their nights; and for the resident, one day and one night."" The narrator added: > **""I traveled with ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه, and he used to wipe over his leather socks for three days.""**"
"1403","Al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtaybah reported from ʿAlī and Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنهما that they said: > **""For the traveler, three days and their nights; and for the resident, one day and one night.""**"
"1404","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: > **""If I were to incur major ritual impurity (janābah) and could not find water for a whole month, I would not pray.""**"
"1405","ʿAlqamah reported: A man was afflicted with smallpox (judarī), so Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه ordered that soil be brought near him in a basin or bowl: > **""And he performed tayammum using the soil.""**"
"1406","ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""I have been granted that which was not given to any of the Prophets."" I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, what is it?"" He ﷺ said: > **""I have been granted victory through awe cast into the hearts of enemies; I have been given the keys of the earth; I have been named Aḥmad; the soil has been made a means of purification for me; and my nation has been made the best of nations.""**"
"1407","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I live in the sand for four or five months, and among us are women experiencing post-natal bleeding, menstruating women, and individuals in a state of sexual impurity (janābah). What do you instruct?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""You must use the soil.""**"
"1408","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Clean earth is the ablution of the Muslim, even if he does not find water for ten years. But whenever he finds water, let him fear Allah and let it touch his skin, for that is better.""**"
"1409","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""I have been granted five things that were not given to any Prophet before me: I was sent to all humanity, the red and the black, whereas every previous Prophet was sent only to his own village; I was aided with awe, my enemy being terrified of me from the distance of a month's journey; the spoils of war were made lawful food for me; the earth was made for me a place of prayer and a means of purification; and I was given intercession, which I have reserved for my nation on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"1410","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said: Abū Dharr رضي الله عنه was tending a small flock of sheep in Medina. When he arrived, the Prophet ﷺ called out to him, ""O Abū Dharr!"" but he remained silent. He called him again, but he remained silent. The Prophet ﷺ said, ""O Abū Dharr, may your mother be bereaved of you!"" He replied, ""Indeed, I am in a state of major ritual impurity (janābah)."" So the Prophet ﷺ called for a maidservant to bring water, and she brought it. Abū Dharr screened himself behind his mount and performed ghusl, then came to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: > **""The clean earth suffices you even if you do not find water for twenty years; but when you find water, let it touch your skin.""**"
"1411","Al-Aslaʿ ibn Sharīk رضي الله عنه said: I used to saddle the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. On a bitter cold night, I incurred major ritual impurity (janābah) while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to set out. I disliked saddling his she-camel while in a state of janābah, yet I feared that if I bathed with cold water I might die or fall ill. Therefore, I asked a man from the Anṣār to saddle it. I then heated stones to warm some water, performed ghusl, and caught up with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his Companions. He ﷺ said, ""O Aslaʿ, why do I see the saddling of your mount has changed?"" I replied, ""O Messenger of Allah, I did not saddle it; a man from the Anṣār saddled it."" He asked, ""And why?"" I said, ""I incurred major impurity and feared the severe cold for myself, so I asked him to saddle it, and I heated stones to warm water and bathed."" Thereupon Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed: > **""{O you who have believed, do not approach prayer while you are intoxicated... [up to His words:] Indeed, Allah is ever Pardoning and Forgiving.}"" [al-Nisāʾ: 43]**"
"1412","Al-Aslaʿ ibn Kaʿb رضي الله عنه—a man from Banū al-Aʿraj—said: I used to serve the Prophet ﷺ. He said to me, ""O Aslaʿ, get up and show me such-and-such."" I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred major ritual impurity."" He remained silent for a while until Jibrīl عليه السلام came down to him with the ruling of tayammum with clean earth. He ﷺ said: > **""Stand, O Aslaʿ, and perform tayammum.""** The sub-narrator said: Then Aslaʿ demonstrated how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught him tayammum: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck the earth with both palms, rubbed them against each other, dusted them off, and then wiped the outer and inner parts of his forearms with them."
"1413","Al-Aslaʿ رضي الله عنه said: I used to serve the Prophet ﷺ and saddle his mount. One night he said to me, ""O Aslaʿ, get up and saddle."" I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred major ritual impurity."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent, and Jibrīl عليه السلام came to him with the verse of clean earth (tayammum). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Get up, O Aslaʿ, and perform tayammum."" So I got up, performed tayammum, and saddled for him. As he traveled, he passed by water and said to me: > **""O Aslaʿ, let this touch your skin.""** The narrator said: ""My father demonstrated tayammum to me just as his father had demonstrated it to him: one strike for the face, and one strike for the arms up to the elbows."""
"1414","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Tayammum consists of one strike for the face, and one strike for the hands up to the elbows.""**"
"1415","Muʿādh ibn Jabal رضي الله عنه said: > **""I used to see the Prophet ﷺ perform tayammum with clean earth, and I only ever saw him wipe his hands and face once.""**"
"1416","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Tayammum consists of two strikes: one strike for the face, and one strike for the hands up to the elbows.""**"
"1417","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Regarding tayammum with clean earth: a person strikes the earth with his palms and wipes his face with them, then strikes once more and wipes his forearms up to the elbows with them.""**"
"1418","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها reported from the Prophet ﷺ regarding tayammum: > **""Two strikes: one strike for the face, and one strike for the hands up to the elbows.""**"
"1419","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ was on a journey. When the time for prayer arrived, the people halted. A shepherd caught sight of them, so he dismounted, struck his hands upon the clean earth, performed tayammum, and then called the Adhān saying, ""Allāhu Akbar, Allāhu Akbar."" The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: > **""He is upon the natural disposition (fiṭrah).""** The shepherd then said, ""Ashhadu allā ilāha illā Allāh"" (I testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah). The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""He has been delivered from the Fire.""**"
"1420","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, if a man is away from settlements and unable to find water, may he have intimate relations with his wife?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""Yes.""**"
"1421","Ḥakīm ibn Muʿāwiyah reported from his uncle, who said: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I remain away from water for a whole month while my wife is with me; may I be intimate with her?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""Yes.""** I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, what if I remain away for several months?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Even if you remain away for three years.""**"
"1422","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out and relieved himself, then wiped with soil (performed tayammum). I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, the water is close to you!"" He ﷺ replied: > **""I do not know; perhaps I might not reach it.""**"
"1423","Sahl ibn Saʿd رضي الله عنه reported: > **""The Companions of the Prophet ﷺ used to go to al-Ghābah (the forest), and the time for Maghrib prayer would overtake them near the sheep enclosure (mirbad al-ghanam), so they would perform tayammum.""**"
"1424","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ رضي الله عنهما reported that ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ رضي الله عنه incurred major ritual impurity while he was commander of the army. He abstained from ghusl, saying: ""If I bathe, I will die of cold."" So he led his companions in prayer while in that state [having performed tayammum]. When he returned to the Prophet ﷺ, he informed him of what he had done and explained his excuse: > **""So the Prophet ﷺ approved his action and remained silent.""**"
"1425","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ led the people in prayer while in a state of janābah [having performed tayammum]. When they returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, they mentioned that to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ summoned him and questioned him about it, to which he said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I feared that the cold would kill me, and Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has said: '{And do not kill yourselves; indeed, Allah is ever Merciful to you.}' [al-Nisāʾ: 29]."" > **""So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent, confirming his action.""**"
"1426","ʿAlqamah reported that a man was afflicted with smallpox. Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه ordered that soil be brought close to him in a basin or bowl: > **""And he performed tayammum with the soil.""**"
"1427","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها said: > **""Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had intimate relations with one of his wives and felt too languid to stand up immediately, he would strike his hand against the wall and perform tayammum.""**"
"1428","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: > **""It is from the Sunnah that a person should not offer more than one prayer with a single tayammum; he must perform tayammum anew for the next prayer.""**"
"1429","ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn رضي الله عنه said: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and a man among the people incurred major ritual impurity. Finding no water, he prayed [with tayammum]. Later, water became available while the time for that prayer still remained, so the man took a bath: > **""And the Prophet ﷺ did not command him to repeat the prayer.""**"
"1430","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported: When Ibn Qamiʾah struck the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Uḥud: > **""I saw the Prophet ﷺ, whenever he performed ablution, loosen his head bandage and wipe over it with the water of ablution.""**"
"1431","ʿItbān—or Ibn ʿItbān—al-Anṣārī رضي الله عنه said: I said, ""O Prophet of Allah, I was with my wife, and when I heard your voice I withdrew immediately and performed ghusl."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Water [ghusl] is only necessitated by water [seminal emission].""**"
"1432","Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called out to me while I was upon my wife. I got up before ejaculating and took a bath. I then informed him, saying, ""You called me while I was upon my wife and had not ejaculated, yet I took a bath."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""No blame upon you; water [ghusl] is only necessitated by water [seminal discharge].""**"
"1433","ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went looking for a man from the Anṣār and called him. The Anṣārī came out with water dripping from his head. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""What is the matter with your head?"" He replied, ""You called me while I was with my wife, and fearing that I would delay you, I hurried, stood up, poured water over myself, and came out."" He ﷺ asked, ""Had you ejaculated?"" He said, ""No."" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whenever you do that, do not take a bath; wash whatever touched the woman from you, and perform ablution as you do for prayer, for water [ghusl] is only necessitated by water [ejaculation].""**"
"1434","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for a man from the Anṣār, and he was slow in coming. He ﷺ asked, ""What kept you?"" The man replied, ""When your messenger came to me, I was upon my wife, so I stood up and took a bath."" He ﷺ said: > **""There was no burden upon you if you did not bathe, as long as you did not ejaculate.""** The narrator said: ""And the Anṣār used to act upon that."""
"1435","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said: The Prophet ﷺ came to the door of a man from the Anṣār and greeted him with Salām while the Anṣārī was upon his wife. He returned the greeting while upon her. The Prophet ﷺ gave Salām a second time, and he returned it but did not stand up. Then the Prophet ﷺ turned to leave when permission was not granted. The man immediately stood up before finishing, and went out following the footsteps of the Prophet ﷺ seeking him. Abū Hurayrah said: We came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was standing, and we gathered around him. The man had bathed in a stream next to his house, and when he approached having bathed, the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""He has taken a bath while ghusl was not obligatory upon him.""** The man came apologizing to the Prophet ﷺ and explained his situation, so the Prophet ﷺ said to him: > **""You took a bath when ghusl was not obligatory upon you.""** And in the narration of al-Bazzār: > **""When one of you approaches his wife and does not ejaculate (aqḥaṭa), then no ghusl is required of him.""**"
"1436","Jābir رضي الله عنه reported: The Prophet ﷺ called a man from the Anṣār, and he was slow to come out. When he emerged, he stated his excuse, so the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""When one of you does not ejaculate (aqḥaṭa) or feels languor without emission (aksala), no ghusl is incumbent upon him.""**"
"1437","ʿUbayd ibn Rifāʿah reported that his father رضي الله عنه said: > **""We used to do that in the era of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: if we did not ejaculate, we would not perform ghusl.""**"
"1438","One of the sons of Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj reported from Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj رضي الله عنه, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called out to me while I was upon my wife. I stood up before ejaculating, took a bath, and went out to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I informed him, saying, ""You called me while I was upon my wife, so I got up before ejaculating and took a bath."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""No blame upon you; water [ghusl] is only necessitated by water [ejaculation].""** Rāfiʿ added: > **""Thereafter, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to perform ghusl.""**"
"1439","Rifāʿah ibn Rāfiʿ رضي الله عنه—who was a participant of the Pledge of al-ʿAqabah and the Battle of Badr—said: I was with ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه when it was said to him, ""Zayd ibn Thābit is issuing fatwas to people in the mosque based on his personal opinion regarding one who has intercourse without ejaculating."" ʿUmar said, ""Bring him to me at once!"" When he was brought, ʿUmar said, ""O enemy of his own soul, have you reached the point of issuing fatwas to people in the Mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ based on your personal opinion?!"" Zayd replied, ""I did not do so; rather, my uncles narrated to me from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" ʿUmar asked, ""Which of your uncles?"" He answered, ""Ubayy ibn Kaʿb, Abū Ayyūb, and Rifāʿah ibn Rāfiʿ."" ʿUmar turned to me and asked, ""What is this young man saying?"" I said, ""We used to do that in the era of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" ʿUmar asked, ""Did you ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it?"" I said, ""We simply used to do it during his time."" ʿUmar then gathered the people [Companions], and they all initially agreed that ""water is only from water,"" except ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib and Muʿādh ibn Jabal رضي الله عنهما, who both said: ""When the circumcised part passes the circumcised part, ghusl becomes obligatory."" ʿAlī said, ""O Commander of the Believers, the most knowledgeable of people concerning this matter are the wives of the Prophet ﷺ."" So ʿUmar sent an inquiry to Ḥafṣah رضي الله عنها, and she replied, ""I have no knowledge of that."" Then he sent to ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها, who said: > **""When the circumcised part passes the circumcised part, ghusl becomes obligatory.""** Upon this, ʿUmar became furious and declared: > **""Let it not reach me that anyone engages in intercourse without performing ghusl except that I shall severely punish him!""** The narrator added: Then they discussed coitus interruptus (al-ʿazl), and they considered it permissible. A man whispered to his companion, so ʿAlī asked, ""What is this whispering?"" One of them said, ""He claims that it is the minor burying alive of infants (al-mawʾūdah al-ṣughrā)."" ʿAlī said: > **""It cannot be considered burying alive until it passes through seven stages: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said: {And certainly did We create man from an extract of clay. Then We placed him as a sperm-drop in a firm lodging...} up to His words: {...so blessed is Allah, the Best of creators.} [al-Muʾminūn: 12-14].""** So the Companions dispersed having agreed with the verdict of ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib that there is no harm in coitus interruptus."
"1440","Muʿādh ibn Jabal رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""When the circumcised part passes the circumcised part, ghusl becomes obligatory.""**"
"1441","ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿĀʾidh said: A man asked Muʿādh ibn Jabal رضي الله عنه about what obligates ghusl from sexual intercourse, about praying in a single garment, and about what is lawful with a menstruating wife. Muʿādh said: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning that, and he said: > **""When the circumcised part passes the circumcised part, ghusl becomes obligatory. As for praying in a single garment, wrap it across your shoulders (tawashshaḥ bihi). And as for what is lawful with a menstruating woman, whatever is above the waist-wrapper (izār) is lawful, though abstaining even from that is more virtuous.""**"
"1442","Ibn al-Simṭ said: I heard Bilāl رضي الله عنه saying: I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, when I have relations with my wife and we separate without my having ejaculated, do I take a bath?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""Yes. I have done that with my wife without ejaculating, and we both took a bath.""**"
"1443","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When the circumcised part passes the circumcised part, ghusl (ritual bath) becomes obligatory.""**"
"1444","ʿAlī, ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, and ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنهم said: > **""When the circumcised part passes the circumcised part, ghusl becomes obligatory.""**"
"1445","Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī reported: ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه was asked about a man who has intercourse with his wife but does not ejaculate. He replied: > **""As for me, whenever I do that with my wife, I perform ghusl.""** Sufyān said: And the consensus of scholars is that ghusl is obligatory."
"1446","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: > **""No prophet ever experienced a wet dream; nocturnal emission is only from Satan.""**"
"1447","Sahlah bint Suhayl رضي الله عنها reported: She asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, must one of us perform ghusl if she experiences a wet dream?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: > **""Yes, if she sees traces of fluid.""**"
"1448","Sahlah bint Suhayl رضي الله عنها reported that she asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a woman who uses a charm to turn her husband's affection toward her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""It is merely a worldly gratification, and she will have no share of reward in the Hereafter.""** She then asked, ""What is your ruling if a woman sees a wet dream in her sleep—must she perform ghusl?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""If she sees fluid, let her perform ghusl.""**"
"1449","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported: Umm Sulaym رضي الله عنها—the mother of Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه—asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying, ""O Messenger of Allah, does a woman see what a man sees in a dream?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: > **""If a woman sees that and discharges fluid, let her perform ghusl.""**"
"1450","Isḥāq ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Abī Ṭalḥah reported from his grandmother Umm Sulaym رضي الله عنها: She was a neighbor of Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ. Umm Sulaym asked: ""O Messenger of Allah, what is your view if a woman dreams that her husband has intercourse with her—must she perform ghusl?"" Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها said, ""May your hands be dusted with earth, O Umm Sulaym! You have disgraced the women before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ!"" Umm Sulaym responded, ""Indeed, Allah is not shy of the truth, and for us to ask the Prophet ﷺ concerning that which is obscure to us is better than remaining in darkness regarding it."" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Rather, may your hands be dusted with earth, O Umm Salamah! Ghusl is obligatory upon her if she finds fluid.""** Umm Salamah said, ""O Messenger of Allah, does a woman have fluid?"" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Then from where else does her child resemble her? Women are indeed the full counterparts of men.""**"
"1451","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a woman who has a wet dream: ""Is ghusl obligatory upon her?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""Yes, if she finds fluid, let her perform ghusl.""**"
"1452","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported: A woman from the Anṣār asked the Prophet ﷺ about a woman who sees in her sleep what a man sees. He ﷺ said: > **""If she sees that, let her perform ghusl.""** ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها said, ""O so-and-so, you have embarrassed the women!"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Leave her be, for indeed the women of the Anṣār are not prevented by shyness from inquiring about understanding the religion.""**"
"1453","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a woman who sees in her sleep what a man sees. The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""If she discharges fluid just as a man discharges, then ghusl is obligatory upon her; but if she does not discharge, then nothing is required of her.""**"
"1454","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, Allah forbids you from being naked; so be shy before the angels of Allah who never part from you except during three states: when relieving oneself, during sexual intimacy (janābah), and when bathing. Therefore, whenever one of you bathes in the open, let him screen himself with his garment, behind a remnant of a wall, or behind his camel.""**"
"1455","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""A person becomes exposed in four situations: when sleeping flat on his back, when sleeping completely alone, when sleeping in a saffron-dyed blanket, and when bathing in an open expanse of land. Whoever is able should not bathe in an open field; but if he must do so, let him draw a line on the ground.""**"
"1456","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ commanded ʿAlī رضي الله عنه, who prepared bathwater for him. The Prophet ﷺ then handed him a garment and said: > **""Screen me and turn your back toward me.""**"
"1457","Umm Hāniʾ رضي الله عنها reported: On the Day of the Conquest of Mecca, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ camped in the upper region of Mecca and I came to him. Abū Dharr رضي الله عنه brought a large bowl containing water—I could even see traces of dough in it. > **""Abū Dharr screened the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he bathed, and then the Prophet ﷺ screened Abū Dharr while he bathed.""**"
"1458","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, whenever Mūsā ibn ʿImrān (Moses) عليه السلام wished to enter the water, he would not cast off his garment until he had concealed his private parts beneath the water.""**"
"1459","Zaynab bint Abī Salamah رضي الله عنها reported: She entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was performing ghusl. He took a handful of water, splashed it toward my face, and said: > **""Stay back, O little girl!""**"
"1460","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bathe behind partitions, and no one ever saw his nakedness.""**"
"1461","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿĀmir ibn Rabīʿah reported from his father, ʿĀmir ibn Rabīʿah رضي الله عنه: He came upon us while we were bathing, pouring water over one another, and said: > **""Do you bathe without screening yourselves?! By Allah, I truly fear that you may be the evil successor generation—meaning the generation in whom evil resides.""**"
"1462","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man from looking at the nakedness (ʿawrah) of his brother.""**"
"1463","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported: > **""He disliked bathing at midday and at the onset of late night (ʿatamah).""**"
"1464","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported: A man asked, ""How much water is sufficient for me for wuḍūʾ?"" He said, ""A mudd."" The man asked, ""How much water is sufficient for me for ghusl?"" He replied, ""A ṣāʿ."" The man said, ""That is not enough for me."" Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: > **""May you be bereft of your mother! It was sufficient for one who was far better than you—the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.""**"
"1465","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pour water over his head three times with his hand. A man said, ""Indeed, my hair is very thick."" Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه replied: > **""The hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was thicker than yours and purer.""**"
"1466","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه was asked by a man about performing ghusl from ritual impurity. He replied, ""Three (handfuls)."" The man said, ""I have abundant hair."" Abū Saʿīd رضي الله عنه said: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had more hair than you and was far purer.""**"
"1467","A man from among the delegation who questioned ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه reported: They said to him, ""We have come to ask you about three matters: a man's voluntary prayer in his house, ghusl from ritual impurity, and what is lawful for a man with his wife when she is menstruating."" ʿUmar said, ""Are you sorcerers? You have asked me about things that no one has asked me about since I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about them! He ﷺ said: > **'A man's voluntary prayer in his house is light; so whoever wishes, let him illuminate his home.' And concerning ghusl, he said: 'For ghusl from ritual impurity, he washes his private parts, performs wuḍūʾ, and then pours water over his head three times.' And concerning the menstruating woman, he said: 'He is permitted whatever is above the waist-sheet (izār).'""**"
"1468","ʿUmayr, the freed slave of ʿUmar, reported: A group from the people of Iraq came to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه. He asked, ""What brought you?"" They said, ""We came to ask you about three things: a man's voluntary prayer in his home—what is it? What is lawful for a man with his wife while she is menstruating? And about ghusl from ritual impurity."" ʿUmar asked, ""Are you sorcerers?"" They replied, ""No, by Allah, O Commander of the Faithful, we are not sorcerers."" He asked, ""Are you soothsayers?"" They replied, ""No."" He said, ""You have asked me about three matters that no one has asked me about since I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before you."" He then narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""As for a man's voluntary prayer in his house, it is light, so illuminate your home as much as you are able. As for the menstruating wife, you are permitted whatever is above the waist-sheet (izār), and you are not permitted what is beneath it. And as for ghusl from ritual impurity: you pour water with your right hand onto your left, then place your hand into the vessel and wash your private parts and whatever impurities have afflicted you; then perform wuḍūʾ just as you do for prayer; then pour water over your head three times, rubbing your head each time.""**"
"1469","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported: The delegation of Thaqīf said, ""O Messenger of Allah, our land is a cold land; what is sufficient for us for ghusl from ritual impurity?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: > **""As for me, I pour water over my head three times.""**"
"1470","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Medina when I was eight years old. My mother took me by the hand and went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying, ""O Messenger of Allah, there is no man or woman among the Anṣār except that they have presented you with a gift; I have nothing to give you except this son of mine; take him, and let him serve you as long as you wish."" So I served the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for ten years. He never struck me, never insulted me, never rebuked me, and never frowned at me. The very first instruction he gave me was: > **""O my son, keep my secrets and you will be a true believer.""** My mother and the wives of the Prophet ﷺ used to ask me about his secrets, but I never informed them, nor will I ever disclose the secrets of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to anyone. And he ﷺ said: > **""O my son, perform wuḍūʾ thoroughly and completely; your two guardian angels will love you and your lifespan will be lengthened. O Anas, be thorough when performing ghusl from ritual impurity, for you will emerge from your bath cleansed of every sin and fault.""** I asked, ""How is thoroughness achieved, O Messenger of Allah?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Moisten the roots of your hair and cleanse the skin. O my son, if you are able to remain in a state of wuḍūʾ at all times, then do so; for whoever is overtaken by death while in a state of wuḍūʾ is granted the reward of martyrdom. O my son, if you are able to remain constantly in prayer, then do so; for the angels send blessings upon you as long as you are praying. O Anas, when you bow (in rukūʿ), place your palms firmly upon your knees, spread your fingers, and keep your elbows away from your sides. O my son, when you raise your head from bowing, let every limb settle in its place; for Allah will not look on the Day of Resurrection at one who does not straighten his spine between his bowing and prostration. O my son, when you prostrate, settle your forehead and palms firmly upon the ground; do not peck like a rooster, and do not squat like a dog—or he said: like a fox. Beware of glancing around in prayer, for glancing around in prayer brings ruin; if it is unavoidable, let it be in voluntary prayer, not in the obligatory prayer. O my son, when you leave your house, do not let your gaze fall upon anyone of the people of the Qiblah without greeting them with Salām, for you will return with your sins forgiven. O my son, when you enter your house, greet yourself and your family with Salām. O my son, if you are able to reach morning and evening without harboring deceit or malice in your heart toward anyone, then do so, for that will ease your reckoning. O my son, if you heed my counsel, nothing will be dearer to you than death.""** And in the narration of al-Ṭabarānī: > **""O my son, when you leave your house, let not your eyes fall upon anyone of the people of the Qiblah except that you deem him superior to you. O my son, that is from my Sunnah; and whoever revives my Sunnah has loved me, and whoever loves me will be with me in Paradise.""**"
"1471","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Six mudds of water are sufficient for ghusl from ritual impurity.""**"
"1472","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported: > **""The Prophet ﷺ used to perform wuḍūʾ with a mudd of water and perform ghusl with a ṣāʿ.""**"
"1473","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: > **""The Sunnah regarding ghusl from ritual impurity is to wash your palms until you cleanse them; then dip your right hand into the vessel and pour with your right hand onto your left, washing your private parts until you cleanse them; then strike your left hand against the wall or the ground and rub it; then pour water over it with your right hand and wash it; then perform wuḍūʾ just as you perform it for prayer.""**"
"1474","Maymūnah bint Saʿd رضي الله عنها reported: She asked, ""Advise us, O Messenger of Allah, concerning ghusl from ritual impurity."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Moisten the roots of the hair and cleanse the skin; for the parable of those who do not perform ghusl thoroughly is like a tree reached by water whose leaves do not sprout and whose root is not quenched. So fear Allah and perform ghusl well, for it is part of the sacred trust (amānah) with which you have been entrusted, and among the concealed matters committed to your charge.""** She asked, ""How much water is sufficient for the head, O Messenger of Allah?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""Three handfuls.""**"
"1475","Umm ʿAṭiyyah رضي الله عنها reported: I was among the women who prepared the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for her marriage, and he ﷺ said: > **""When you pour water over her head, pour it three times in the ghusl from ritual impurity.""**"
"1476","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported: > **""Whenever he performed ghusl, he would open his eyes and insert his finger into his navel (to ensure water reached it).""**"
"1477","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها reported: I had tied my hair very tightly, so the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""O ʿĀʾishah, do you not know that under every single hair there is ritual impurity?""**"
"1478","Sālim, the servant of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, reported: > **""The wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to braid their hair into four plaits; when they performed ghusl, they would gather them in the center of their heads without undoing them.""**"
"1479","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When a woman performs ghusl following menses, she should undo her hair and wash it with marsh mallow (khiṭmī) and potash (ushnān); but when she performs ghusl from ritual impurity (janābah), she pours water over her head and squeezes it.""**"
"1480","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه reported: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about a man who performs ghusl from ritual impurity, but water misses a portion of his body. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""He should wash that specific spot and then pray.""**"
"1481","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: > **""When one of you performs ghusl while in ritual impurity using marsh mallow (khiṭmī), and then performs ghusl after that, he may wash his head with water if he wishes.""**"
"1482","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه reported: > **""He used to wash his head with marsh mallow (khiṭmī) while in ritual impurity, and then perform ghusl on the rest of his body without rewashing his head.""**"
"1483","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: > **""If a person in ritual impurity washes his head with marsh mallow (khiṭmī), he has done so thoroughly, and it will not harm him if he does not pour water over it afterward.""**"
"1484","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever performs wuḍūʾ after ghusl is not of us.""**"
"1485","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported: > **""The Prophet ﷺ and his wife—or he said: one of his wives—used to perform ghusl together from a single vessel.""**"
"1486","Maymūnah رضي الله عنها reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Wuḍūʾ is not to be performed using the leftover water of a woman's ghusl from ritual impurity.""**"
"1487","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Let no person who is in ritual impurity sleep until he has performed wuḍūʾ.""**"
"1488","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported: > **""Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in ritual impurity and wished to eat or sleep, he would perform wuḍūʾ.""**"
"1489","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها reported: > **""Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered a state of ritual impurity, he would not eat until he performed wuḍūʾ.""**"
"1490","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها reported: > **""Whenever the Prophet ﷺ wished to sleep while in ritual impurity, he would perform wuḍūʾ just as he did for prayer; and whenever he wished to eat, he would wash his hands.""**"
"1491","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها reported: > **""Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had relations with one of his wives and felt too sluggish to rise, he would strike his hands against the wall and perform tayammum.""**"
"1492","Mālik ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ghāfiqī رضي الله عنه reported: One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate food, then said, ""Screen me so that I may perform ghusl."" I asked, ""Were you in ritual impurity, O Messenger of Allah?"" He replied, ""Yes."" I reported that to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه, who came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, ""This man claims that you ate while in ritual impurity!"" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Yes; whenever I perform wuḍūʾ, I may eat and drink, but I neither recite the Qur'an nor pray until I perform ghusl.""**"
"1493","ʿAbdullāh ibn Mālik al-Ghāfiqī رضي الله عنه reported: One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate food, then said, ""Screen me so that I may perform ghusl."" I said to him, ""Were you in ritual impurity, O Messenger of Allah?"" He replied, ""Yes."" I reported that to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه, who came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""This man claims that you ate while in ritual impurity?"" He ﷺ said: > **""Yes; whenever I perform wuḍūʾ, I eat and drink.""**"
"1494","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما reported: > **""Whenever the Prophet ﷺ wished to sleep while in a state of ritual impurity, he would perform wuḍūʾ.""**"
"1495","ʿAdī ibn Ḥātim رضي الله عنه reported: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning a person in ritual impurity: ""May he sleep?"" He ﷺ said: > **""He should perform wuḍūʾ just as he performs it for prayer.""**"
"1496","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported: > **""The Prophet ﷺ granted a concession to a person in ritual impurity, when wishing to eat or sleep, to perform wuḍūʾ.""**"
"1497","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, the angels do not attend to a person in ritual impurity nor one heavily smeared with saffron perfume (khalūq) until both perform ghusl.""**"
"1498","Maymūnah bint Saʿd رضي الله عنها reported: I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, may one of us eat while in ritual impurity?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""He should not eat until he performs wuḍūʾ.""** I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, may a person in ritual impurity sleep?"" He ﷺ said: > **""I do not like that he should sleep while in ritual impurity until he performs wuḍūʾ; for indeed, I fear that should he pass away, Jibrīl (Gabriel) عليه السلام will not attend to him.""**"
"1499","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها reported: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would enter a state of ritual impurity, then sleep, then awaken, and then sleep again (before performing ghusl).""**"
"1500","Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī رضي الله عنه reported: Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out and saw any of his Companions, he would stroke his face and supplicate for him. One day he went out and met Ḥudhayfah رضي الله عنه, but Ḥudhayfah slipped away from him. When he later came to him, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked, ""O Ḥudhayfah, I saw you, but then you turned away?"" He said, ""Because I was in a state of ritual impurity."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed, a Muslim never becomes impure.""**"
"1501","Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān رضي الله عنه reported: > **""The Prophet ﷺ shook hands with me while I was in a state of ritual impurity.""**"
"1502","Ibn Jurayj reported: I was informed that ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه: > **""Used to warm himself with his wife during winter while she was in ritual impurity and he had performed ghusl, and he would seek coolness with her in summer while both were in that state.""**"
"1503","Al-Ḥakam ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When one of you performs ghusl and then something (fluid) emerges from his private part, let him perform wuḍūʾ.""**"
"1504","ʿAbdullāh ibn Ḥanẓalah رضي الله عنه reported: > **""A man greeted the Prophet ﷺ with Salām shortly after he had urinated, but the Prophet ﷺ did not return his greeting until he struck his hand against the wall—meaning that he performed tayammum.""**"
"1505","Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib رضي الله عنه reported: > **""He greeted the Prophet ﷺ with Salām while he was urinating, and he did not return the greeting until he had finished.""**"
"1506","Jābir ibn Samurah رضي الله عنه reported: I came upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was urinating, and I greeted him with Salām, but he did not respond to me. Then he entered his house, performed wuḍūʾ, came out, and said: > **""And upon you be peace (Wa ʿalaykumu al-Salām).""**"
"1507","Abū Sallām reported from someone who saw the Prophet ﷺ: > **""He urinated, and then recited verses from the Qur'an before touching water.""**"
"1508","ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib and Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Do not recite the Qur'an while you are in a state of ritual impurity.""** The narrator said: I said to ʿAlī, ""Indeed, the Prophet ﷺ used to recite the Qur'an in all circumstances except when in ritual impurity."""
"1509","ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib رضي الله عنه reported: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform wuḍūʾ and then recite a portion of the Qur'an. He ﷺ said: > **""This is for one who is not in ritual impurity; as for the one in janābah, no—not even a single verse.""**"
"1510","ʿAlqamah ibn al-Faghwāʾ رضي الله عنه reported: Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed water, we would speak to him and he would not speak to us, and we would greet him with Salām and he would not return it to us, until he entered his house and performed wuḍūʾ as for prayer. We said, ""O Messenger of Allah, we speak to you and you do not speak to us, and we greet you with Salām and you do not return it to us?"" [This continued] until the verse of concession was revealed: > **""{O you who have believed, when you rise to [pray] prayer...} [Al-Māʾidah: 6].""**"
"1511","Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī reported: ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه was teaching a man to recite the Qur'an. When he reached the bank of the Euphrates, he urinated, and the man refrained from reciting. Ibn Masʿūd asked, ""What is the matter with you?"" He said, ""You have broken your wuḍūʾ."" Ibn Masʿūd said: > **""Recite!"" So the man began reciting, and Ibn Masʿūd continued prompting and correcting him.**"
"1512","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""None shall touch the Qur'an except one who is pure.""**"
"1513","Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām رضي الله عنه reported: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched me to Yemen, he said: > **""Do not touch the Qur'an unless you are pure.""**"
"1514","Al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah reported that ʿUthmān ibn Abī al-ʿĀṣ رضي الله عنه—who was a young man—said: We came as a delegation to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they found that I had memorized the most Qur'an among them, having surpassed them by virtue of Sūrah al-Baqarah. The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""I have appointed you as leader over your companions even though you are the youngest of them; and do not touch the Qur'an unless you are pure.""**"
"1515","The Judge of the Armies at Constantinople reported that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه addressed the people, saying: ""O people, indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him never sit at a dining spread upon which wine is circulated; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not enter the public bath except wearing a waist-sheet (izār); and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not allow his wife to enter the public bath.""**"
"1516","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day among the men of my nation, let him not enter the public bath except wearing a waist-sheet (miʾzar); and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not allow his wife to enter the public bath.""**"
"1517","Umm al-Dardāʾ رضي الله عنها reported: I came out from the public bath, and the Prophet ﷺ met me and said, ""From where have you come, O Umm al-Dardāʾ?"" I said, ""From the public bath."" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""By the One in Whose hand is my soul, there is no woman who takes off her garments in other than the house of one of her mothers except that she has torn down every veil between herself and the Most Merciful—Exalted and Majestic is He.""**"
"1518","Al-Sāʾib, the freed slave of Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها, narrated that some women from the people of Ḥimṣ entered upon Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها. She asked them, ""Where are you from?"" They replied, ""From the people of Ḥimṣ."" She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Any woman who takes off her clothes anywhere other than her own home, Allah tears down her veil of modesty.""**"
"1519","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Beware of an establishment called the public bath (al-ḥammām).""** They said, ""O Messenger of Allah, it cleanses dirt."" He ﷺ said: > **""Then conceal your private parts (when entering).""**"
"1520","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day must not enter the public bath except wearing a waist-wrap; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day must not allow his wife to enter the public bath; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should hasten to the Friday prayer. And whoever disregards it out of amusement or trade, Allah will disregard him, and Allah is Self-Sufficient, Praiseworthy.""**"
"1521","Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his neighbor; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day must not enter the public bath except wearing a waist-wrap; and whoever among your women believes in Allah and the Last Day must never enter the public bath.""**"
"1522","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها narrated that she asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about public baths, and he said: > **""There will soon be public baths after my time, and there is no good in public baths for women.""** She asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, even if she enters wearing a waist-wrap?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""No, even if she enters wearing a waist-wrap, a tunic, and a veil. For no woman removes her veil outside the house of her husband except that she tears away the veil between herself and her Lord.""**"
"1523","Al-Miqdām ibn Maʿdīkarib رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""You will soon conquer distant horizons wherein there are houses called public baths; entering them is forbidden for my Ummah.""** They said, ""O Messenger of Allah, they relieve ailment and cleanse dirt."" He ﷺ said: > **""Then they are permissible for the males of my Ummah wearing waist-wraps, but forbidden for the females of my Ummah.""**"
"1524","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The worst house is the public bath: voices are raised in it and nakedness is uncovered.""** A man said, ""O Messenger of Allah, the sick are treated in it and dirt is removed."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: > **""Then whoever enters it must not enter except fully covered.""**"
"1525","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Do not enter the public bath except wearing a waist-wrap. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day must not let his wife enter the public bath; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day must not drink wine; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day must not sit at a dining table upon which wine is consumed; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day must never be in seclusion with a woman unless there is a maḥram with her.""**"
"1526","Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The first person for whom depilatory paste (al-nūrah) was made and who entered public baths was Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd عليهما السلام. When he entered it and felt its heat and suffocating vapor, he said: 'Ah, from the punishment of Allah! Ah, ah, before it is of no avail! Ah, ah, ah!'""**"
"1527","Abū Rāfiʿ رضي الله عنه narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a certain place and said: > **""What an excellent location for a bathhouse this is.""** And subsequently, a public bath was built there."
"1528","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day must not enter the public bath except wearing a waist-wrap.""**"
"1529","It is narrated regarding ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما: He entered the public bath, and the bath attendant applied depilatory paste to him. When the attendant reached his waistline, he said to the attendant: > **""Step outside.""**"
"1530","Sukayn ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated from his father, who said: I entered upon ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما while a slave-girl was shaving his hair, and he said: > **""Indeed, depilatory paste thins the skin.""**"
"1531","Al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated: I heard al-Awzāʿī say: > **""The thigh is ʿawrah in the mosque, but in the public bath it is not considered ʿawrah.""**"
"1532","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about semen that soils a garment. He ﷺ said: > **""It is only of the status of mucus or spittle; remove it from yourself with a rag or lemongrass (idhkhir).""**"
"1533","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها said: > **""I used to scrape the semen from the garment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.""**"
"1534","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: > **""We used to scrape it off with lemongrass (idhkhir) and tufts of wool""—meaning semen.**"
"1535","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The minimum duration of menstruation is three days, and its maximum is ten days.""**"
"1536","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The menstruating woman observes her condition up to ten days: if she sees purity, then she is pure; but if the bleeding exceeds ten days, she has irregular bleeding (istiḥāḍah)—she must perform ghusl and pray. If the blood overwhelms her, she should apply a pad of cotton, strap it securely, and perform wuḍūʾ for every prayer. And the woman experiencing postpartum bleeding (nufasāʾ) observes up to forty days: if she sees purity before that, she is pure; but if it exceeds forty days, she is treated as a woman with irregular bleeding—she performs ghusl and prays, and if the blood overwhelms her, she applies a pad of cotton, straps it securely, and performs wuḍūʾ for every prayer.""**"
"1537","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه said: > **""Let the menstruating woman wait five, seven, eight, nine, or ten days; once ten days have elapsed, she is considered to have irregular bleeding (mustaḥāḍah).""**"
"1538","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Menstruation occurs in surges, and menstrual blood has a distinctive scent by which it is recognized. So when the menstrual period has passed, let each of you perform ghusl and wash the blood from herself.""**"
"1539","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها narrated that Fāṭimah bint Abī Ḥubaysh questioned the Prophet ﷺ, saying, ""I experience continuous irregular bleeding."" He ﷺ said: > **""Abandon prayer during the days of your regular menstruation, then perform ghusl and make wuḍūʾ for every prayer, even if the blood drips onto the reed mat.""**"
"1540","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما narrated that the Prophet ﷺ was asked about a woman suffering from irregular bleeding, and he said: > **""That is merely a spur from the spurs of Satan struck into her womb.""**"
"1541","Jābir رضي الله عنه narrated that Fāṭimah bint Qays رضي الله عنها asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning a woman with irregular bleeding, and he said: > **""She remains seated during the days of her regular periods, then performs ghusl at every attainment of purity, then applies a pad of cotton and prays.""**"
"1542","Jābir رضي الله عنه reported from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: > **""He commanded the woman suffering from irregular bleeding (istiḥāḍah) to perform wuḍūʾ for every prayer.""**"
"1543","Sawdah bint Zamʿah رضي الله عنها narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The woman suffering from irregular bleeding refrains from prayer during the days of her regular periods in which she used to abstain, then performs a single ghusl, and thereafter performs wuḍūʾ for every prayer.""**"
"1544","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The woman suffering from irregular bleeding performs ghusl from one menstrual period to the next.""**"
"1545","Jābir رضي الله عنه narrated: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed a limit of forty days for women with postpartum bleeding.""**"
"1546","ʿUthmān ibn Abī al-ʿĀṣ رضي الله عنه said: > **""Forty days was fixed as the limit for women with postpartum bleeding.""**"
"1547","ʿĀʾidh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنه—who was among those who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ beneath the tree—narrated that his wife gave birth and experienced postpartum bleeding. She saw signs of purity after twenty days and took a bath. She then came to enter beneath his quilt, and feeling her touch, he asked, ""Who is this?"" She replied, ""So-and-so."" He asked, ""What is your condition?"" She replied, ""I saw signs of purity and took a bath."" Thereupon, he nudged her away with his foot, removing her from his bed, and said: > **""Do not seduce me away from my religion until forty days have fully passed!""**"
"1548","ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar narrated that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه said: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, ""What is lawful for a man from his wife while she is menstruating?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""Whatever is above the waist-wrap (izār).""**"
"1549","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما narrated that a man asked: ""O Messenger of Allah, what is permissible for me with my wife while she is menstruating?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""She should fasten her waist-wrap securely, and then you may enjoy whatever else of her you wish.""**"
"1550","ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: ""What is lawful for a man from his wife while she is menstruating?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""Whatever is above the waist-wrap; and whatever is beneath the waist-wrap is unlawful.""**"
"1551","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما narrated: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I had intercourse with my wife while she was menstruating."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him: > **""Free a slave (as expiation).""** And the price of a slave in those days was one dinar."
"1552","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما narrated: While Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها was lying down one night with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, she slipped away discreetly. He ﷺ asked: > **""What is the matter with you? Have you started your menses?""** She replied, ""Yes."" He ﷺ said: > **""There is no harm; put on your menstrual wrap, and then return to your place.""**"
"1553","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها narrated: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to avoid intimacy during the initial surge of menstrual blood for three days, and thereafter he would be affectionate.""**"
"1554","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه narrated that Khawlah bint Yasār came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I have only a single garment, and I menstruate in it."" He ﷺ said: > **""When you become pure, wash the place where the blood struck, and then pray in it.""** She asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, what if its stain does not disappear?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""Water is sufficient for you, and its remaining stain will not harm you.""**"
"1555","Khawlah bint Ḥakīm رضي الله عنها said: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I menstruate and have only a single garment."" He ﷺ said: > **""Wash it and pray in it.""** I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, a trace of blood remains on it."" He ﷺ replied: > **""It does not harm you.""**"
"1556","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها said: > **""One of us would menstruate in her garment, and when the day of her purity arrived, she would wash whatever blood had touched it and pray in it. Yet today, one of you dedicates her maidservant solely to washing her clothes on the day she becomes pure!""**"
"1557","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said to ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها: > **""Hand me the small prayer mat (al-khumrah) from the mosque.""** She said, ""I am in a state of ritual impurity (menstruating)."" He ﷺ said: > **""Is your menstruation in your hand?""**"
"1558","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said to ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها: > **""Hand me the prayer mat.""** She said, ""I am menstruating."" He ﷺ replied: > **""Indeed, your menstruation is not in your hand.""**"
"1559","Abū Bakrah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said to his maidservant: > **""Hand me the prayer mat from the mosque.""** She said, ""I am menstruating."" He ﷺ said: > **""Hand it to me nonetheless.""**"
"1560","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه narrated that Thumāmah ibn Uthāl (or Uthālah) accepted Islam, whereupon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Take him to the orchard of Banū so-and-so, and instruct him to perform ghusl with water and lote leaves (sidr).""**"
"1561","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه narrated: > **""When Thumāmah ibn Uthāl embraced Islam, the Prophet ﷺ instructed him to perform ghusl and pray two rakʿahs.""**"
"1562","Wāthilah ibn al-Asqaʿ رضي الله عنه narrated: When I embraced Islam, I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to me: > **""Perform ghusl with water and lote leaves (sidr), and cast off from yourself the hair of disbelief.""**"
"1563","Qatādah Abū Hishām رضي الله عنه narrated: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said to me: > **""O Qatādah, perform ghusl with water and lote leaves (sidr), and shave off the hair of disbelief.""** And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command whoever embraced Islam to be circumcised, even if he were eighty years of age."
"1564","ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir رضي الله عنه narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw me while I was serving water to two men from a small leather jug in front of me. I cleared my throat and spat, and some of my phlegm landed on my garment. I began washing my garment using water from the jug before me, whereupon the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""O ʿAmmār, your phlegm and the tears of your eyes are nothing other than like the pure water in your vessel. You only need to wash your garment from urine, feces, semen (al-māʾ al-aʿẓam), blood, and vomit.""**"
"1565","ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir رضي الله عنه narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw me by a well drawing water into a leather jug of mine, so he asked, ""What are you doing?"" I replied, ""O Messenger of Allah, I am washing my garment from major ritual impurity (janābah) that touched it."" He ﷺ said: > **""O ʿAmmār, a garment is only washed from feces, urine, vomit, and blood.""**"
"1566","Maʿqil ibn Yasār رضي الله عنه narrated: ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān رضي الله عنه used to experience great hardship from prostatic fluid (al-madhy), so he dispatched a man to the Prophet ﷺ to ask about it. The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""That is madhy, and every virile man discharges madhy. Wash it off with water, perform wuḍūʾ, and pray.""**"
"1567","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه narrated: ʿAlī رضي الله عنه dispatched a man to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to ask him concerning madhy, as he felt shy to ask him personally due to his marriage to Fāṭimah رضي الله عنها. The man asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, a man sees a woman and discharges madhy; is ghusl obligatory upon him?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""That is something experienced by virile men; for that, performing wuḍūʾ suffices you.""**"
"1568","Abū Laylā رضي الله عنه narrated: I was with the Prophet ﷺ while al-Ḥasan or al-Ḥusayn عليهما السلام was upon his chest or stomach, and the child urinated. I saw the streams of his urine flowing, and we rushed forward toward him, but the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Leave my son; do not startle him until he completes his urination.""** Then he poured water over it. He then stood up and entered the storage room of charity dates accompanied by the boy. The boy took a date and put it into his mouth, but the Prophet ﷺ took it out and said: > **""Indeed, charity is not lawful for us.""**"
"1569","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما narrated: Umm al-Faḍl bint al-Ḥārith رضي الله عنها brought Umm Ḥabībah bint al-ʿAbbās and placed her in the lap of the Prophet ﷺ, and the infant girl urinated. Umm al-Faḍl snatched her away abruptly and struck her between her shoulders. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Hand me a cup of water.""** He then poured it over the area of her urine, and said: > **""Pour water wherever urine has reached.""**"
"1570","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه narrated: While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was resting on his back in one of his houses, al-Ḥasan came toddling along until he sat upon the chest of the Prophet ﷺ and urinated on his chest. I stepped forward to remove him, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ awoke and said: > **""Woe to you, O Anas! Leave my son and the fruit of my heart alone, for whoever harms him harms me, and whoever harms me harms Allah.""** Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water and poured it copiously over the urine, saying: > **""Water is poured over the urine of a boy, and the urine of a girl is washed.""**"
"1571","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه narrated: Al-Ḥusayn رضي الله عنه was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he began kissing him while he was in his lap. The infant urinated, and the people moved to take him away, but he ﷺ said: > **""Leave him.""** And he left him until he had completely finished urinating."
"1572","Zaynab bint Jaḥsh رضي الله عنها narrated: The Prophet ﷺ was sleeping in her quarters while al-Ḥusayn was crawling around the room. She momentarily became distracted from him, and he crawled over until he reached the Prophet ﷺ, climbed onto his stomach, and urinated upon his navel. She said: The Prophet ﷺ woke up, so I rushed toward him and took him off his stomach, but the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Leave my son.""** When he finished urinating, he took a jug of water and poured it over it, then said: > **""Water is poured over the urine of a boy, whereas the urine of a girl is washed.""**"
"1573","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما narrated: > **""A male baby was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and urinated on him, so he sprinkled water over it; and a female baby was brought and urinated on him, so he washed it.""**"
"1574","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها narrated: Al-Ḥasan or al-Ḥusayn urinated on the stomach of the Prophet ﷺ, whereupon the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Do not abruptly interrupt my son (or: do not rush him).""** He left him until he had completed urinating, then called for water and poured it over it."
"1575","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""If the boy has not yet begun eating solid food, water is poured over his urine; but if it is a girl, it is washed.""**"
"1576","Al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī narrated: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه intended to forbid Tamattuʿ in Hajj, but Ubayy ibn Kaʿb رضي الله عنه said to him, ""That is not for you to do; we performed Tamattuʿ with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" ʿUmar also intended to prohibit the garments of al-Ḥīrah because they were dyed using urine, but Ubayy said to him: > **""That is not for you to do; the Prophet ﷺ wore them, and we wore them during his lifetime.""**"
"1577","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: > **""We used to pray alongside the Prophet ﷺ and we did not perform wuḍūʾ on account of anything stepped on.""**"
"1578","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه narrated: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not perform wuḍūʾ on account of anything he stepped upon.""**"
"1579","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه narrated: A Bedouin came and urinated in the mosque. The Prophet ﷺ ordered concerning that spot, so it was dug out and a bucket of water was poured over it. The Bedouin said, ""O Messenger of Allah, a man loves a people yet has not attained their deeds?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""A person will be with the one whom he loves.""**"
"1580","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported a similar narration from the Prophet ﷺ regarding the Bedouin who urinated in the mosque: > **""The Prophet ﷺ ordered that the spot be dug out and that a bucket of water be poured over it.""**"
"1581","Nāfiʿ narrated: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما was asked concerning walled enclosures (orchards) wherein there is filth, human urine, and animal dung. He said: > **""When rains have flowed over it and winds have dried it, there is no harm in praying in it.""** He mentioned that as tracing back to the Prophet ﷺ."
"1582","ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib رضي الله عنه narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Jibrīl عليه السلام came to me but did not enter. The Prophet ﷺ asked him: 'What prevented you from entering?' He replied: 'Indeed, we do not enter a house wherein there is an image or urine.'""**"
"1583","Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Purify your courtyards, for indeed the Jews do not clean their courtyards.""**"
"1584","ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Were it not that dogs are a community among communities, I would have ordered them all to be killed; so kill from among them every jet-black dog. And whoever keeps a dog for other than hunting, guarding crops, or herding livestock, a Qīrāṭ of sin the size of Mount Uḥud is incurred by him every day. And when a dog licks from the vessel of any of you, let him wash it seven times, one of which should be with soil (baṭḥāʾ).""**"
"1585","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه narrated: The Prophet ﷺ used to visit the residence of a certain household of the Anṣār while bypassing a house before them. This caused them distress, so they said, ""O Messenger of Allah, you visit the house of so-and-so but you do not visit our house?"" The Prophet ﷺ replied: > **""Because there is a dog in your house.""** They said, ""Indeed, in their house there is a cat!"" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The cat is a predatory beast (whose roaming does not negate purity in that manner).""**"
"1586","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""When a dog laps from a vessel, it must be washed seven times.""**"
"1587","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When a dog laps from the vessel of one of you, he must wash it seven times—and I believe he said—one of them with earth (dust).""**"
"1588","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما narrated: > **""I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ on a donkey called Yaʿfūr and I perspired, so the Prophet ﷺ instructed me to perform ghusl.""**"
"1589","Abū al-Zubayr narrated: I asked Jābir رضي الله عنه concerning a mouse that dies in food or drink, ""May I eat it?"" He replied: > **""No; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ strictly forbade that.""**"
"1590","Maymūnah رضي الله عنها, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated that she sought a ruling from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning a mouse that had fallen into solid clarified butter (ghee) belonging to them. He ﷺ said: > **""Cast it away and whatever surrounds it, and eat your clarified butter.""**"
"1591","Abū al-Dardāʾ رضي الله عنه narrated that a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""A mouse fell into the gravy (stew)."" He ﷺ said: > **""Cast it away from you, then scoop out three handfuls with both your hands, and then eat it.""**"
"1592","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a mouse that fell into clarified butter. He ﷺ said: > **""Throw it away and what is around it, and eat it if it is solid.""** They asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, what if it is liquid?"" He ﷺ replied: > **""Benefit from it (for non-edible purposes).""**"
"1593","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه narrated: The Prophet ﷺ was asked concerning dough into which drops of blood had fallen, whereupon: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade eating it.""**"
"1594","Abū ʿUbaydah narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Satan passed before me, so I seized him and choked him until I truly felt the coolness of his tongue upon my hand, whereupon he cried: 'You have hurt me! You have hurt me!'""**"
